hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1201","24 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that Umar shared among them and said: I will not deprive them if they gain extra closeness."
"1202","25 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn al-Muntashir informed me, he said: I witnessed Masruq and Shurayh sharing among them."
"1203","26 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali that he used to give the third to the maternal brothers and sisters to the exclusion of the full brothers and sisters; and Zayd ibn Thabit used to do that. Hushaym said: So I objected to that, saying: Zayd used to share among them. He said: But al-Sha'bi narrated to us from him that he said as Ali said. So I said: Between me and you is Ibn Abi Layla."
"1204","27 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, he said: I asked Abu al-Zinad about the opinion of Zayd on that, so Abu al-Zinad said: Zayd used to share among them."
"1205","28 - Sa'id said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, that there was an inheritance case among them: a woman left her husband, her mother, her maternal siblings and her full siblings, so Ibn Mas'ud said: For the husband half, for the mother a sixth, and for her maternal siblings what remains; the shares are exhausted. Huzayl said: So we mentioned that to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, and he said: Do not ask me about anything while this learned scholar is among you."
"1206","29 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, that a man died leaving his daughter, his son's daughter, and his full sister, so they came to al-Ash'ari and asked him about that, and he said: For his daughter half, and the remaining half for the sister. Then they came to Ibn Mas'ud and mentioned that to him, so Abdullah said: I would have gone astray then, and I would not be among the guided, if I took the opinion of al-Ash'ari and abandoned the opinion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then he said: For the daughter half, for the son's daughter a sixth, and what remains is for the sister."
"1207","30 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: I heard al-Aswad ibn Yazid saying: Mu'adh ruled in Yemen regarding a daughter and a sister with half and half."
"1208","31 - Sa'id said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from al-Aswad, he said: When Mu'adh came to Yemen he was asked about a daughter and a sister, so he gave the daughter half and gave the sister half."
"1209","32 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Masruq, from Ash'ath ibn Sulaym, he said: I heard al-Aswad saying: So I mentioned that to Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr and he said: You are my messenger to Abdullah ibn Utbah that he should rule with that."
"1210","Chapter on increase (al-awl). 33 - Sa'id said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Thabit that he was the first to apply increase in the inheritance shares, and the most the increase ever reached was like two-thirds of the head of the estate."
"1211","34 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: Ali was approached regarding a man who died leaving his two parents, his two daughters and his wife, so Ali said to the wife: I see your eighth has become a ninth."
"1212","35 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ibn Abbas said: No estate increases."
"1213","36 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Do you think that the One who counted the sand of Alij in number put in one wealth a half, a third and a fourth? Rather, it is two halves, three thirds and four fourths."
"1214","37 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: People take neither my opinion nor yours, and if you and I died they would never divide an inheritance according to what we say. He said: Let them gather, and let us place our hands on the Corner, then let us supplicate and make the curse of Allah upon the liars: Allah did not rule with what they said."
"1215","Chapter of the grandfather. 38 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd informed us, he said: al-Hasan narrated to us, that Umar ibn al-Khattab adjured the people, saying: Whoever among you has knowledge from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the grandfather, let him stand. So Ma'qil ibn Yasar al-Muzani stood and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled regarding a grandfather who was among us. He said: How much did he give him? He said: He gave him a sixth. He said: With whom? He said: I do not know. He said: Then you do not know."
"1216","39 - Sa'id said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Isa ibn Abi Isa al-Hannat, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab asked the people: Which of you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say anything regarding the grandfather? A man said: I did. He said: What did he give him? He said: He gave him a sixth of his wealth. He said: Who was with him among the heirs? He said: I do not know. He said: Then you do not know. Another said: I have knowledge, O Commander of the Faithful. What did he give the grandfather? He gave him a third of his wealth. He said: Who was with him among the heirs? He said: I do not know. He said: Then you do not know. Another said: I have knowledge. What did he give him? He gave him half of his wealth. He said: Who was with him among the heirs? He said: I do not know. He said: Then you do not know. Another said: I have knowledge. What did he give him? He said: He gave him all the wealth. He said: Who was with him among the heirs? He said: I do not know. He said: Then you do not know. Then when Zayd ibn Thabit laid down the inheritance shares, he gave him a sixth of his wealth with a male child, gave him a third of his wealth with siblings, gave him half of his wealth with one brother, and gave him all the wealth when he had no heir."
"1217","40 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, he said: Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that Abu Bakr used to treat the grandfather as a father."
"1218","41 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that Abu Bakr made the grandfather a father."
"1219","42 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Abu Bakr used to treat the grandfather as a father."
"1220","43 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Abu Burdah, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, from Uthman ibn Affan, that Abu Bakr used to make the grandfather a father."
"1221","44 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah al-Darir narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari: Make the grandfather a father, for Abu Bakr made the grandfather a father."
"1222","45 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur and Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that Abu Bakr used to treat the grandfather in the standing of the father."
"1223","46 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Ata, that Abu Bakr, Uthman and Ibn Abbas used to make the grandfather a father; and Ibn Abbas said: My son inherits from me to the exclusion of my brother, and I do not inherit from my son to the exclusion of his brother."
"1224","47 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, that Abu Bakr made the grandfather a father."
"1225","48 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, he said: As for the one about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were to take an intimate friend from this community I would have taken Abu Bakr - he ruled him to be a father."
"1226","49 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The grandfather is a father; and he recited: {And I have followed the religion of my fathers, Ibrahim, Ishaq and Ya'qub}."
"1227","50 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that he used to say: Whoever wishes, I will invoke mutual curse with him at the Black Stone that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not mention in the Qur'an any grandfather or grandmother; they are but fathers. Then he recited: {And I have followed the religion of my fathers, Ibrahim, Ishaq and Ya'qub}."
"1228","51 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Juwaybir informed us, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to him asking him about the grandfather, so he said: What is your name? He said: So-and-so. He said: Son of whom? He said: Son of so-and-so. He said: Son of whom? He said: Son of so-and-so. So he said: I do not see you counting but fathers. Then he recited this verse: {And I have followed the religion of my fathers, Ibrahim, Ishaq and Ya'qub}. He said: So he began with his two grandfathers before his father."
"1229","52 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-A'mash informed us, he said: Imran ibn al-Harith al-Sulami narrated to us, he said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and asked him about the grandfather, so he said: What is your name? He said: So-and-so. He said: Son of whom? He said: Son of so-and-so. He said: Son of whom? He said: Son of so-and-so. He said: I do not see you counting but fathers."
"1230","Chapter on the opinion of Umar regarding the grandfather. 53 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, he said: Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated to us, he said: A grandson of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, died, leaving his grandfather Umar and his brothers, so Umar sent to Zayd ibn Thabit, and Zayd began calculating, so Umar said to him: Speak confusedly? You were never one to confuse; by my life, I know that I am more entitled to him than they."
"1231","54 - Sa'id said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Shinzhir, he said: I heard al-Hasan saying: If I were put in charge of anything of the people's affairs, I would treat the grandfather as a father."
"1232","55 - Sa'id said: Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The boldest of you in dividing the grandfather's share is the boldest of you toward the Fire."
"1233","56 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated to us, he said: A shaykh from Murad informed me, from Ali, that he said: Whoever is pleased to plunge into the masses of Hell, let him judge between the grandfather and the siblings."
"1234","57 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from a shaykh from Murad, from Ali, the like of it."
"1235","58 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Awf informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to an agent of his: Give the grandfather with one brother half, with two brothers a third, with three a fourth, with four a fifth, and with five a sixth; if they are more than that, do not reduce him below a sixth."
"1236","59 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Ubayd ibn Nudaylah, he said: Umar and Abdullah used to share the grandfather with the siblings so long as a sixth was better for him than sharing with the siblings; then Umar wrote to Abdullah: I do not see but that we have been unfair to the grandfather, so when this letter of mine reaches you, share him with the siblings so long as a third is better for him than sharing with them; so Abdullah adopted that."
"1237","60 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Umar wrote to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari: We had given the grandfather with the siblings a sixth, and I think we were but unfair to him; so when this letter of mine reaches you, give the grandfather with one brother half, and with two brothers a third, and if they are more than that, do not reduce him below a third."
"1238","61 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Zayd informed us, from Shu'bah ibn al-Taw'am al-Dabbi, he said: A brother of ours died in the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab, leaving his grandfather and his siblings, so we came to Ibn Mas'ud and he gave the grandfather with the siblings a sixth; then another brother of ours died in the time of Uthman, leaving his grandfather and his siblings, so we came to Ibn Mas'ud and he gave the grandfather with the siblings a third. We said: Did we not come to you regarding our first brother and you gave the grandfather with the siblings a sixth, then now you give him a third? So Abdullah said: We only rule with the rulings of our leaders."
"1239","62 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Simak ibn al-Fadl, from Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam, that Umar ibn al-Khattab was approached regarding an inheritance case and he assigned it; then in the following year I witnessed him approached regarding that same case and he assigned it otherwise. I said: I witnessed you last year assigning it otherwise. He said: That was upon what we assigned, and this is upon what we assign."
"1240","63 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us - he once said: from a man, without mentioning the report, then he dictated it to us without mentioning a man - he said: Mu'awiyah wrote to Zayd ibn Thabit asking him about the grandfather, so Zayd wrote to him: Allah knows best about the grandfather; I witnessed the two caliphs before you, and they used to give the grandfather with one brother half, and with two brothers a third, and if they were more than that they did not reduce them below a third."
"1241","64 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah, he said: The grandfather shares with the siblings so long as it does not fall below a third; when the siblings gather, the grandfather is given a third and the siblings are given what remains. And he used to give the grandfather with a son a sixth."
"1242","65 - Sa'id said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Ali, regarding a husband, a mother, a full sister and a grandfather. He said: Ali said regarding it: For the husband three shares, for the mother two shares, for the grandfather one share, and for the sister three shares. And Ibn Mas'ud said: For the husband three shares, for the mother one share, for the grandfather one share, and for the sister three shares. And Zayd ibn Thabit said regarding it: For the husband three shares, for the mother two shares, for the grandfather one share, and for the sister three shares; then he multiplies all the shares by three, making twenty-seven shares: for the husband of that nine, for the mother six, and twelve shares remain: for the grandfather of that eight, and for the sister four."
"1243","66 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from Ali, Abdullah and Zayd ibn Thabit, the like of that; and Hushaym added from Ibn Abbas: For the husband half, for the mother a third, for the grandfather what remains, and the sister gets nothing."
"1244","67 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ali, Abdullah, Zayd and Ibn Abbas, the like of that."
"1245","68 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Ali, Abdullah and Zayd, the like of that."
"1246","69 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: Umar and Abdullah did not prefer a mother over a grandfather."
"1247","70 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from Ali regarding a man who left his grandfather, his mother and his sister: he gave the sister half, the mother a third, and the grandfather a sixth; and that Ibn Mas'ud gave the sister half, the mother a sixth, and the grandfather a third; and that Zayd ibn Thabit made it from nine: he gave the mother a third, and made what remained between the grandfather and the sister, for the male the like of the share of two females."
"1248","71 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Ubaydah, from al-Sha'bi, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf was approached regarding this inheritance case and sent to me, saying: What do you say regarding it? I said: What is it? He said: A mother, a grandfather and a sister. I said: What did the commander say regarding it? He told me his opinion, so I said: This is the ruling of Abu Turab - meaning Ali ibn Abi Talib - and seven of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke regarding it: Umar ibn al-Khattab and Ibn Mas'ud said regarding it: For the sister half, for the mother a sixth, and for the grandfather a third. And Ali said regarding it: For the mother a third, for the sister half, and for the grandfather a sixth. And Uthman ibn Affan said: For the mother a third, for the sister a third, and for the grandfather a third. So al-Hajjaj said: This is nothing. And Zayd ibn Thabit said regarding it: It is from nine shares: for the mother three shares, for the grandfather four, and for the sister two shares. And Ibn Abbas and Ibn al-Zubayr said regarding it: For the mother a third, for the grandfather what remains, and the sister gets nothing."
"1249","72 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah, regarding a daughter, a sister and a grandfather, he said: He gave the daughter half, and made what remained between the grandfather and the sister, half for him and half for her."
"1250","73 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah was asked about a daughter, two sisters and a grandfather, and he said: For the daughter half, and he made what remained between the grandfather and the two sisters, half for him and half for the two of them."
"1251","74 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah was asked about a daughter, three sisters and a grandfather: he gave the daughter half, gave the grandfather two-fifths of what remained, and gave the sisters a fifth each. [Flag: the division wording is ambiguous in the source; rendered literally.]"
"1252","75 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah did not share paternal brothers with full brothers, nor paternal sisters with full sisters."
"1253","76 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: Ali did not give the grandfather with a child more than a sixth."
"1254","77 - Sa'id said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali, regarding a daughter, a sister and a grandfather, he said: For the daughter half, for the grandfather a sixth, and what remains is for the sister."
"1255","78 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Whoever claims that any of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave maternal siblings inheritance along with a grandfather has lied."
"1256","Chapter of the grandmothers. 79 - Sa'id said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, Hammad ibn Zayd and Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave three grandmothers a sixth to share; and Jarir added: Mansur said: So I said to Ibrahim, and he said: His father's two grandmothers - his mother's mother and his father's mother - and the mother's mother's mother. [Flag: chain is mursal; rendered literally.]"
"1257","80 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, he said: The grandmother came to Abu Bakr after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: My son's son - or my daughter's son - died, and I have been told that I have a right in the Book of Allah. So Abu Bakr said: I do not find for you any right in the Book of Allah, nor did I hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rule anything for you; but I shall ask the people. So he asked the people, and al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her a sixth. He said: Who testifies with you? He said: Muhammad ibn Maslamah. So they both testified, and he gave her a sixth. Then the one opposed to her - the mother's mother or the father's mother - came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he gave her a sixth; then he said: Whichever of you two is alone, it is hers, and if you both come together, it is between you."
"1258","81 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, he said: Two grandmothers came to Abu Bakr, and he gave the mother's mother to the exclusion of the father's mother; so Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl - who was a Badri - said to him: You have given the one whom, had she died, he would not have inherited from. So he made the sixth between them."
"1259","82 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, that a man died leaving his two grandmothers - his mother's mother and his father's mother - so they came to Abu Bakr, and he gave his mother's mother the sixth and left the father's mother. So a man from the Ansar said to him: You have given inheritance to a woman whom, had she been the deceased, he would have inherited nothing from, and you have left a woman whom, had she been the deceased, he would have inherited all her wealth. So he shared the sixth between them."
"1260","83 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, from Qatadah, from Ibn Sirin that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a grandmother a sixth, and she was from Khuza'ah. [Flag: chain is mursal; rendered literally.]"
"1261","84 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla and al-Ash'ath informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Ali and Zayd used to give inheritance to three grandmothers: two from the father's side and one from the mother's side, and they used to give the sixth to the nearest of them."
"1262","85 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim: Abdullah said: None excludes the grandmothers except the mother."
"1263","86 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan that he used to give inheritance to three of the grandmothers: two from the father's side and one from the mother's side; and Ibn Sirin used to give inheritance to four when their kinship was equal."
"1264","87 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Sawwar informed us, he said: al-Sha'bi narrated to us, he said: Four grandmothers came to Masruq disputing, so he cast out the father's mother's mother. He said: So I told that to Ibn Sirin, and he said: Abu A'ishah erred; are they all given inheritance together?"
"1265","88 - Sa'id said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Shinzhir, from Ata, that Zayd ibn Thabit said: A man excludes his mother as the mother excludes her mother from the sixth."
"1266","89 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Dawud, from Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: I cast out the father's mother's mother only because the mother's father does not inherit."
"1267","90 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Maysarah informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that Umar ibn al-Khattab gave a grandmother of a man from Thaqif inheritance along with her son."
"1268","91 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salim narrated to us, he said: al-Sha'bi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah used to give inheritance to three grandmothers: two from the father's side and one from the mother's side, and he used to make the sixth among them so long as one of them did not inherit to the exclusion of another, the one from the father's side."
"1269","92 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, that Ali and Zayd used to give the sixth to the nearer of them."
"1270","93 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad: he heard his shaykhs Talhah, Kharijah and Sulayman ibn Yasar saying: When the grandmother from the mother's side is nearer, she is more entitled to it."
"1271","94 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: They used to give inheritance to three of the grandmothers: two grandmothers from the father's side and one from the mother's side."
"1272","95 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from Ibn Sirin, he said: I was told that the first grandmother given a sixth to share was a father's mother along with her son."
"1273","96 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, from al-Hasan that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a grandmother inheritance along with her son. [Flag: chain is mursal; rendered literally.]"
"1274","97 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin that they both used to give the grandmother inheritance along with her son."
"1275","98 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim that he used to give the grandmother inheritance along with her son."
"1276","99 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Mas'ud that the first grandmother given a sixth to share was a father's mother along with her son."
"1277","100 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla and Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Ali and Zayd did not give her inheritance."
"1278","101 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Fudayl ibn Amr, from Ibrahim, from Ali and Zayd, the like of that."
"1279","102 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Alqamah informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal al-Adawi, from a man among them, that a man among them died leaving his two grandmothers - his mother's mother and his father's mother - while his father was alive, so I took charge of his estate and gave the sixth to his mother's mother and left the father's mother. It was said to me: You should have shared between them. So I came to Imran ibn Husayn and asked him about that, and he said: Share the sixth between them. So I did."
"1280","103 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that a man from Banu Hanzalah called Hasakah: a son of his died, leaving his father Hasakah and his father's mother, so that was raised to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, and he wrote regarding that to Umar ibn al-Khattab, so Umar wrote to him: Give Hasakah's mother inheritance from Hasakah's son along with her son Hasakah."
"1281","104 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Humayd al-Himyari informed us, from his father, from al-Ash'ari and Umar, the like of that."
"1282","105 - Sa'id said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Shinzhir, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, that al-Ash'ari gave Hasakah's mother inheritance from a son of Hasakah while Hasakah was alive."
"1283","106 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Humayd informed us, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin that they both used to give her inheritance along with her son."
"1284","107 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid and Mansur informed us, from Anas ibn Sirin, he said: I witnessed Shurayh approached regarding a man who left his two grandmothers - his father's mother and his mother's mother - while his father was alive, and he shared the sixth between his two grandmothers."
"1285","108 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Anas ibn Sirin, that Shurayh gave a grandmother inheritance along with her son."
"1286","109 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, he said: Ibn Mas'ud gave a grandmother inheritance along with her son."
"1287","110 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Ibn Mas'ud said: The first grandmother to inherit in Islam along with her son."
"1288","111 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir ibn Zayd, he said: A grandmother inherits along with her son."
"1289","Chapter on what has come regarding return (al-radd). 112 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah did not return upon six: he did not return upon a husband, nor upon a wife, nor upon a grandmother, nor upon maternal siblings along with a mother, nor upon son's daughters along with loin daughters, nor upon paternal sisters along with full sisters. Ibrahim said: So I said to Alqamah: Do you return upon maternal siblings along with a grandmother? He said: If you wish. And Ali used to return upon all of them except the husband and the wife."
"1290","113 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed, he said: al-Sha'bi narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit never returned anything upon the relatives; he used to give the fixed-sharers their shares and put what remained into the public treasury when there was no agnate."
"1291","114 - Sa'id said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, he said: I saw my father returning the excess wealth beyond the fixed shares to the public treasury, and not returning anything upon an heir."
"1292","115 - Sa'id said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Ali used to return the surplus upon every heir in proportion to what he inherited, except the husband and the wife."
"1293","116 - Sa'id said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Ibn Mas'ud used to return the surplus upon every heir in proportion to what he inherited, except that he did not return upon a son's daughter along with a loin daughter, nor upon a paternal sister along with a full sister, nor upon a grandmother unless there was another heir with her, nor anything upon a maternal sister along with a mother, nor upon the husband, nor upon the wife."
"1294","117 - Sa'id said: Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Ibn Mas'ud gave the maternal siblings a third, and gave the rest of the wealth to the mother, saying: She is the agnate of one who has no agnate."
"1295","118 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: The mother is the agnate of one who has no agnate, and the sister is the agnate of one who has no agnate."
"1296","119 - Sa'id said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Salim, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali, that he said regarding the son of a woman subjected to mutual cursing (mula'anah) who died leaving his mother and his brother: For his brother a sixth, for his mother a third, and what remains is returned upon them in proportion to their shares. And Abdullah said: For his brother a sixth, and what remains is for his mother; and he said: She is his agnate. And Zayd ibn Thabit said: For his mother a third, for his brother a sixth, and what remains is for the public treasury."
"1297","120 - Sa'id said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali and Ibn Mas'ud: they both said regarding the child of mutual cursing: His mother is his agnate, and if he has no mother then her agnate is his agnate; and the child of adultery is like the child of mutual cursing."
"1298","Chapter on what has come regarding the hermaphrodite. 121 - Sa'id said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Amr ibn Harim, from Jabir ibn Zayd, he said: Ziyad was brought a man who had a vulva and a penis, and he did not know how to give him inheritance, so he said: Who is there for this? They said: Jabir ibn Zayd. So he sent to him while he was detained in prison; he came dragging in his shackles and said: Speak regarding him. He said: Stick him to a wall: if he urinates upon it, he is a man, and if he urinates upon his feet, he is a female."
"1299","122 - Sa'id said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I mentioned the opinion of Jabir ibn Zayd to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, so Sa'id said: What if he urinates from both together? I said: I do not know. He said: From whichever of them comes first."
"1300","123 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr informed us, from Jabir ibn Zayd, that Ziyad had imprisoned him on suspicion, and a dispute regarding the hermaphrodite was brought to Ziyad, so Ziyad sent to Jabir asking him how to give him inheritance. So Jabir said: They suspect us and imprison us, yet ask us about what befalls them of their religion's affairs. Then he sent to him that he be given inheritance according to his urination."
"1301","124 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mujalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Mu'awiyah was approached regarding the hermaphrodite, so he asked those before him, and he ordered that he be given inheritance according to his urination."
"1302","125 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, he said: A shaykh from Fazarah narrated to me, he said: I heard Ali saying: Praise be to Allah who made our enemy ask us about what befell him of his religion's affair; Mu'awiyah wrote to me asking me about the hermaphrodite, so I wrote to him that he be given inheritance according to his urination."
"1303","126 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali, the like of that."
"1304","Chapter on what has come regarding two paternal cousins, one of whom is a maternal brother. 127 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ziyad, the freedman of Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, he said: Ibn Mas'ud was approached regarding two paternal cousins, one of whom is a maternal brother, and he said: The wealth is for the maternal brother."
"1305","128 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to me, he said: Ali was approached regarding two paternal cousins, one of whom is a maternal brother, and they said to him: Ibn Mas'ud gave the wealth to the maternal brother? He said: May Allah have mercy on him; he was indeed learned - if only he had given the maternal brother a sixth and divided what remained between them."
"1306","129 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Ibn Mas'ud was consulted about a woman who left two paternal cousins, one of whom was her husband and the other her maternal brother. Abdullah said: The husband gets one-half, and what remains goes to the maternal brother. Ali and Zayd said: The husband gets one-half, the maternal brother gets one-sixth, and what remains is divided between them."
"1307","130 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Aws ibn Thabit al-Ansari informed us, from Hakim ibn Iqal, that Shurayh was consulted about a woman who left two paternal cousins, one her husband and the other her maternal brother. He assigned one-half to the husband and the remaining half to the maternal brother. They went to Ali and mentioned that to him, so he sent for Shurayh. When he came to him he said: How did you judge among these people? He informed him of his judgment. He said to him: What led you to that? He said: The statement of Allah Almighty: And blood relatives are more entitled to one another in the Book of Allah. Ali said to him: Why did you not give the husband his ordained share in the Book of Allah, one-half, and give the brother his ordained share, one-sixth, and make what remains between them in halves?"
"1308","131 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Shurayh, that he judged likewise, and the husband said: I am an agnate (asaba) like this one. Shurayh said: Were it not that you are a husband, I would not have given you anything."
"1309","Chapter: The agnates when one of them is closer. 132 - Sa'id said: Abu Awanah narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: Umar said: If the agnates are of one category and one of them is closer through the mother, give him the entire estate."
"1310","133 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, he said: al-A'mash narrated, from Shaqiq, he said: A letter from Umar ibn al-Khattab reached us: If some agnates are closer through the mother, hand over to him the entire estate."
"1311","134 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, he said: al-A'mash narrated, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: If among the agnates one is closer through the mother, give him the entire estate."
"1312","Chapter: People of two religions do not inherit from one another. 135 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Muslim does not inherit from the disbeliever, nor does the disbeliever inherit from the Muslim."
"1313","136 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: People of two religions do not inherit from one another. Sa'id said: Hushaym said: I heard it, or he informed me from him."
"1314","137 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Ya'qub ibn Ata, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People of two differing religions do not inherit from one another."
"1315","138 - Sa'id said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Anas ibn Sirin who said: Umar said: People of two differing religions do not inherit from one another, and one who does not inherit does not exclude (others)."
"1316","139 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Juwaybir informed us, from al-Dahhak, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People of two differing religions do not inherit from one another."
"1317","140 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: People of two differing religions do not inherit from one another."
"1318","141 - Sa'id said: Abu Awanah and Hushaym narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: We do not inherit from the people of (other) religions, nor do they inherit from us."
"1319","142 - Sa'id said: Abu Waki' narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali who said: The Muslim does not inherit from the disbeliever unless he is his slave."
"1320","143 - Sa'id said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali who said: The Muslim does not inherit from the disbeliever."
"1321","144 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, he said: al-Sha'bi narrated that al-Ash'ath ibn Qays came as a delegate to Umar ibn al-Khattab concerning the inheritance of a Jewish paternal aunt of his. When he came to him, Umar said to him: Have you come to me about the inheritance of al-Mughzilla bint al-Harith? He said: Am I not the most entitled of people to her? He said: The people of her religion, of her faith, are (entitled); people of two religions do not inherit from one another."
"1322","145 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Dawud reported, from al-Sha'bi who said: It reached Mu'awiyah that some Arabs were kept from Islam by the matter of their inheritance from their fathers. Mu'awiyah said: We inherit from them but they do not inherit from us. Masruq ibn al-Ajda' said: No judgment introduced in Islam is more pleasing to me than it."
"1323","146 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mujalid informed us, he said: al-Sha'bi narrated, he said: A man came to Mu'awiyah and said: Do you think Islam harms me or benefits me? He said: Rather it benefits you; what is the matter? He said: His father was a Christian, and his father died upon his Christianity while I am a Muslim, and my brothers, who are Christians, say: We are more entitled to our father's inheritance than you. Mu'awiyah said: Bring them to me. He brought them to him, and he said: You and he share equally in the inheritance of your father. And Mu'awiyah wrote to Ziyad: Give the Muslim a share of inheritance from the disbeliever, but do not give the disbeliever a share from the Muslim. When his letter reached Ziyad, he sent for Shurayh and ordered him to give the Muslim inheritance from the disbeliever and not to give the disbeliever inheritance from the Muslim. Before that Shurayh used to give neither the disbeliever from the Muslim nor the Muslim from the disbeliever; when Ziyad ordered him, he judged by his word, and whenever he judged thus he would say: This is the judgment of the Commander of the Believers."
"1324","147 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi who said: When Mu'awiyah judged as he judged concerning that, Abdullah ibn Ma'qil said: No judgment introduced in Islam after the judgment of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is more pleasing to me than the judgment of Mu'awiyah: We inherit from them but they do not inherit from us, just as marriage is lawful for us among them but is not lawful for them among us."
"1325","148 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, he said: al-A'mash narrated, from Ibrahim who said: Ali would not exclude (heirs) on account of a Jew, a Christian, a Magian, or a slave, nor would he give them inheritance; and Abdullah would exclude on account of them but would not give them inheritance."
"1326","149 - Sa'id said: Abu Shihab narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz freed a Christian slave of his, and he died leaving wealth, so Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ordered that what he left be placed in the public treasury."
"1327","150 - Sa'id said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that he was asked about a boy whose mother was a slave and whose grandmother, his mother's mother, was free, and he died. He said: His grandmother inherits from him."
"1328","151 - Sa'id said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from his father who said: The view of the jurists who were the final authority was that the slave does not inherit and is not counted for exclusion, that the disbeliever neither inherits nor is counted for exclusion, and that one whose (order of) death is obscure neither inherits nor is counted for exclusion."
"1329","152 - Sa'id said: Khalid narrated, from Khalid, from Ibn Sirin, concerning a Muslim who freed a Christian and then he died. He said: He does not inherit from him."
"1330","Chapter: The paternal aunt and the maternal aunt. 153 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah and Abu Shihab narrated, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, that Umar ibn al-Khattab gave the paternal aunt two-thirds and the maternal aunt one-third."
"1331","154 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from al-Sha'bi who said: A case of a paternal aunt and a maternal aunt reached Ziyad, and Ziyad said: I am the most knowledgeable of people about the judgment of Umar ibn al-Khattab concerning them: he put the paternal aunt in the position of the father and gave her two-thirds, and he put the maternal aunt in the position of the mother and gave her one-third."
"1332","155 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, he said: al-Sha'bi narrated, from Masruq ibn al-Ajda', from Ibn Mas'ud, that he said: The paternal aunt is in the position of the father, the maternal aunt is in the position of the mother, the brother's daughter is in the position of the brother, and every blood relative is in the position of the womb-tie through which he connects, when there is no (ordained) heir or fixed share."
"1333","156 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that Masruq judged concerning a paternal aunt and a maternal aunt: he put the paternal aunt in the position of the father and gave her two-thirds, and he put the maternal aunt in the position of the mother and gave her one-third. Ibrahim said: And Abdullah used to say that."
"1334","157 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that a man recognized a sister of his who had been taken captive in the pre-Islamic period; he found her with a son of hers whose father was unknown. He bought them both and then freed them. The boy acquired some wealth and died. They went to Ibn Mas'ud and mentioned that. He said: Go to the Commander of the Believers, Umar, and ask him about that, then return and inform me of what he says to you. He went to Umar and mentioned that to him, and he said: I do not see you as an agnate nor as one with a fixed share. He returned to Ibn Mas'ud and informed him. Ibn Mas'ud set out until he entered upon Umar and said: How did you rule for this man? He said: I did not see him as an agnate nor as one with a fixed share. Abdullah said: You have neither given him inheritance on account of kinship nor given him inheritance on account of clientage. He said: What do you think? He said: I consider him a blood relative and a benefactor patron, and I think you should give him inheritance. He said: Then he gave him inheritance."
"1335","158 - Sa'id said: Khalid narrated, from Bayan, from Wabarah, from Umar and Abdullah, with this hadith."
"1336","159 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, he said: al-A'mash narrated, from Ibrahim who said: Umar gave a maternal uncle the entire estate, and he was both a maternal uncle and a freed client."
"1337","160 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani informed us, he said: It was said to al-Sha'bi: Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah judged concerning a man who left his daughter or his sister, giving her the entire estate. Al-Sha'bi said: One better than Abu Ubaydah used to do that; Ibn Mas'ud used to do it."
"1338","161 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, he said: al-Shaybani informed us, from al-Sha'bi who said: I asked him whether the brother's daughter or the paternal aunt has priority, and he said: The brother's daughter. I bear witness that Masruq said: Put them in the positions of their fathers."
"1339","162 - Sa'id said: Abu Awanah narrated, from Sulayman al-Shaybani who said: I said to Amir al-Sha'bi: Is the paternal aunt or the brother's daughter more entitled to inheritance? He said: And do you not know? The brother's daughter. I bear witness that Masruq said: Put them in the positions of their fathers."
"1340","163 - Sa'id said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me, from Ata ibn Yasar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode to Quba seeking Allah's guidance about the paternal aunt and the maternal aunt, and it was revealed to him that they have no inheritance."
"1341","164 - Sa'id said: Abu Shihab narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi' ibn Habban who said: Thabit ibn al-Dahdahah died leaving no heir and no agnate, and his case was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Asim ibn Adi about him: Has he left anyone? He said: He has not left anyone, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave his estate to his sister's son, Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir."
"1342","165 - Sa'id said: Abu Awanah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, that Umar and Ibn Mas'ud used to give inheritance to the paternal aunt and the maternal aunt when there was no one else."
"1343","166 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim who said: Abdullah said: The mother is the agnate of one who has no agnate, and the sister is the agnate of one who has no agnate."
"1344","167 - Sa'id said: Attab ibn Bashir narrated, from Khusayf, from Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam who said: A man died in the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab leaving only a paternal aunt and a maternal aunt, and Umar gave the paternal aunt two-thirds and the maternal aunt one-third."
"1345","168 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from al-Nadr ibn Shafi, from Imran ibn Sulaym, that a man withdrew from his wealth, and his sister's daughter came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking for the inheritance. He said: You have nothing; O Allah, whoever is deprived is deprived; O Allah, whoever is deprived is deprived. [Flag: the phrase rendered withdrew from his wealth is obscure in the source.]"
"1346","169 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah who said: One with a fixed share is more entitled than one with no share."
"1347","170 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, Damrah ibn Habib, Makhul, and Atiyyah ibn Qays, from Zayd ibn Thabit who said: Neither the sister's son, nor the brother's daughter, nor the paternal cousin's daughter, nor the maternal uncle, nor the paternal aunt, nor the maternal aunt inherits."
"1348","171 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the patron of one who has no patron, and the maternal uncle is the heir of one who has no heir."
"1349","172 - Sa'id said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, he said: Shu'bah narrated, from Budayl ibn Maysarah who said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talhah narrating from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Abu Amir al-Hawzani, from al-Miqdam, a man of the people of Syria who was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever leaves a destitute dependent, his care is upon us; whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs. I am the heir of one who has no heir: I pay his blood-money liability on his behalf and I inherit from him. And the maternal uncle is the heir of one who has no heir: he pays his blood-money liability on his behalf and inherits from him."
"1350","Chapter: Inheritance of the freed client alongside (other) heirs. 173 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, from al-Shaybani, from Ubayd ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had who said: The daughter of Hamzah freed a man; he died leaving his daughter and the daughter of Hamzah. His daughter took one-half and the daughter of Hamzah took one-half, and that was in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1351","174 - Sa'id said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, he said: Shu'bah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad who said: The daughter of Hamzah was my sister through my mother; she freed a slave of hers, and the slave died leaving his daughter and the daughter of Hamzah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave his daughter one-half and the daughter of Hamzah one-half."
"1352","175 - Sa'id said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, he said: Shu'bah narrated, from al-Mughirah who said: Ibrahim used to mention this hadith and say: It was only a gift of food with which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fed her."
"1353","176 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, from al-Shaybani, from al-Hakam, from Shamus, that she brought a case before Ali ibn Abi Talib about her father who died leaving her and leaving his freed clients. Ali gave her one-half and gave his freed clients one-half."
"1354","177 - Sa'id said: Hammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Himmani narrated, from Abu Husayn who said: A woman of Kindah narrated to me that a brother of hers died leaving no one but her and no one but his freed clients. I went to Ali and said: My brother has died leaving no one but me and no one but our freed client. He said: The estate is between you two in halves."
"1355","178 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn Salim informed us, he said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, and a dispute was brought to him about a woman who died leaving her husband, her daughter, and her agnates. Al-Qasim said: The husband gets one-fourth, and what remains goes to the daughter; and he gave the agnates nothing. Then they went to Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab, who was the governor of Kufa at that time, and he gave the husband one-fourth, the daughter one-half, and the remaining fourth to the agnates."
"1356","179 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn Salim narrated to us, he said: I witnessed al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman when a dispute was brought to him about a boy who died leaving his freed clients and his mother. Al-Qasim said to his mother: You carried him in your belly and nursed him at your breast; the entire estate is yours."
"1357","180 - Sa'id said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab used to give inheritance to blood relatives to the exclusion of the freed clients. It was said: Did Ali give them that? He said: Ali was the strictest of them in that."
"1358","181 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, he said: al-A'mash narrated, from Ibrahim who said: Umar and Ibn Mas'ud used to give inheritance to blood relatives to the exclusion of the freed clients. It was said: And Ali? He said: He was the strictest of them in that."
"1359","182 - Sa'id said: Abu Awanah narrated, from Mughirah who said: A freedwoman of Ibrahim died, and some kin of hers through the women came, and he gave her his inheritance. She began praising him, and he said: Had I known I had any right to it, I would not have given it to you."
"1360","Chapter: One who becomes Muslim before the inheritance is divided. 183 - Sa'id said: Abu Awanah narrated, from Adham al-Sadusi, from men of his people, that a Christian woman among them had a Hanif (Muslim) daughter; the daughter died and the mother became Muslim before the inheritance was divided. They went to one of the judges of Basra, who gave her inheritance. Then they went to Kufa and went to Ali and mentioned that to him. He said: What was the mother when the soul left the daughter? They said: A Christian. He said: The inheritance has become due to its (rightful) people, but she has a right; how much is the estate? They said: Such-and-such amount, which Adham did not remember; so he gave her a siqayah (a drink-portion). [Flag: the amount is uncertain in the printed sources.]"
"1361","184 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Adham Abu Bishr al-Sadusi informed us, he said: People of the clan narrated to me that a woman among them died while she was a Hanif (Muslim), leaving her mother who was a Christian; her mother became Muslim before her daughter's inheritance was divided. They went to Ali and asked him about that. Ali said: Did her daughter not die while her mother was a Christian? They said: Yes. He said: Then she has no inheritance; how much did her daughter leave? They informed him, and he said: Give her some of it. So they gave her some of it."
"1362","185 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from Yazid ibn Qatadah al-Shaybani, that he witnessed Uthman ibn Affan giving inheritance to a man who became Muslim before the inheritance was divided."
"1363","186 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: Whoever becomes Muslim before the inheritance is divided gets his share, and whoever is freed before the inheritance is divided gets his share."
"1364","187 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr, from Abu al-Sha'tha who said: If a man dies leaving an enslaved son, and he is freed before his inheritance is divided, he gets his inheritance."
"1365","188 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib who said: Return the dead person('s share) to his family."
"1366","189 - Sa'id said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever becomes Muslim with something in his possession, it is his."
"1367","190 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever becomes Muslim with something in his possession, it is his."
"1368","191 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Ibn Mas'ud, that he used to say about a man who dies leaving his father enslaved: He is bought from the estate, then freed, and what remains is inherited."
"1369","192 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every inheritance which Islam reaches while it has not been divided is divided according to the division of Islam."
"1370","193 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every inheritance divided in the pre-Islamic period stands upon the division of the pre-Islamic period, and every inheritance not divided until Islam reached it stands upon the division of Islam."
"1371","194 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Awsajah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man died in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with no heir except a boy of his whom he had freed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him his inheritance."
"1372","195 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata who said: A blacksmith died in the quarter of Banu Jumah leaving no kin except a slave whom he had freed, and Umar ordered that he be given the estate."
"1373","196 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that every inheritance divided in the pre-Islamic period stands upon the division of the pre-Islamic period, and whatever inheritance Islam reaches stands upon the division of Islam."
"1374","197 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Za'idah ibn Abd al-Rahman, the brother of Banu Sa'idah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged thus among them."
"1375","198 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi who said: Whoever affiliates himself with a people is one of them."
"1376","199 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan who said: Whoever adopts a religion is of its people."
"1377","200 - Sa'id said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya al-Sadafi narrated to us, from al-Qasim al-Shami, from Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever accepts Islam at a man's hands, his clientage belongs to him."
"1378","201 - Sa'id said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, he said: al-Ahwas ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Sa'd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever accepts Islam at a man's hands, he is his client: he inherits from him and pays (blood-money) on his behalf."
"1379","202 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, he said: al-Ahwas ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Sa'd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who accepts Islam at a man's hands. He said: He is the most entitled of people to him: he inherits from him and pays blood-money on his behalf."
"1380","203 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Mawhab, the judge of Palestine, from Tamim al-Dari who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who accepts Islam at a man's hands, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is the most entitled of people to him in his life and after his death."
"1381","204 - Sa'id said: Abu Awanah narrated, from Mansur who said: I asked Ibrahim about a Nabataean who becomes Muslim and affiliates with a man. He said: He inherits from him and pays blood-money on his behalf."
"1382","205 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Abu Malik al-Kufi informed us, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, that he used to say: If he pays blood-money on his behalf, he inherits from him; if he does not pay blood-money on his behalf, he does not inherit from him."
"1383","206 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mutarrif informed us, from al-Sha'bi who said: He was asked about a man who accepts Islam at a man's hands: does he inherit from him? He said: No, not at all, except for one who conferred a favor (of manumission); his wealth is for the Muslims, and his blood-money liability, I think, is upon them."
"1384","207 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan who said: No, except for one who conferred a favor (of manumission)."
"1385","208 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, the same."
"1386","209 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, he said: I asked Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah about a man who accepts Islam at a man's hands. He said: Amr ibn Shu'ayb informed me that Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to Amr ibn al-As: You wrote asking me about people who entered Islam in the early shelter of Islam and died; he said: The wealth of those is to be raised to the treasury of the Muslims. And you wrote asking me about a man who becomes Muslim and joins with a people in alliance and mutual blood-money liability, having no kinship among them nor any favor (of manumission) owed to them; make his inheritance for those with whom he allied and shared liability. [Flag: some words are unclear in the printed source.]"
"1387","210 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz judged concerning a man of those who died leaving his daughter and the sons of his freed patrons: he divided the inheritance between his daughter and the sons of his freed patrons."
"1388","211 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Sha'bi and al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, concerning a man who becomes Muslim and affiliates with a people: they get his inheritance, and his criminal liability is upon them."
"1389","212 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Ibn Mas'ud, the same."
"1390","213 - Sa'id said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, concerning a man of the land who accepts Islam at a man's hands. He said: He gets his inheritance and pays blood-money on his behalf."
"1391","214 - Sa'id said: Jarir narrated, from Mughirah, from Hammad who said: He may move away from him if he wishes, so long as he has not paid blood-money on his behalf; once he has paid blood-money on his behalf, he may not move to another."
"1392","Chapter: A man with no heir may place his wealth wherever he wishes. 215 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from Amr ibn Shurahbil who said: Abdullah said: You, the assembly of Hamdan, are among the most prudent clans in Kufa; one of you dies leaving no agnate, and when that is so, let him bequeath all his wealth."
"1393","216 - Sa'id said: Abu Waki' narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Maysarah - Sa'id said: he is Amr ibn Shurahbil - who said: Abdullah said to me: O Abu Maysarah, among you, the assembly of Hamdan, a dead man dies whose agnate is unknown; when that is so, let him place his wealth wherever he wishes."
"1394","217 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, he said: al-A'mash narrated, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Amr ibn Shurahbil who said: Abdullah said to me: You, the assembly of the people of Yemen, are among the most likely people for a man among you to die leaving no agnate; when that is so, let a man place his wealth wherever he wishes."
"1395","218 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that Ibn Mas'ud said to Abu Ma'mar: O Abu Ma'mar, you, the assembly of the people of Yemen, are such that a dead man dies among you whose agnate is unknown; when one of you is so, let him bequeath all his wealth wherever he wishes."
"1396","219 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus, Hisham, Ibn Awn, and Mansur informed us, from Ibn Sirin who said: I said to Abidah: A man with no known agnate and no covenant owed to anyone - may he bequeath all his wealth? He said: Yes, if he wishes."
"1397","220 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin who said: I asked Abidah about a man who has made no alliance with anyone and has no known agnate: may he bequeath all his wealth? He said: He may bequeath all his wealth if he wishes."
"1398","221 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, the same."
"1399","222 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, that Masruq used to say about one to whom no one owes a favor: He may bequeath all his wealth if he wishes."
"1400","Chapter: Inheritance of the sa'ibah (freedman released with no claim). 223 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Abu Bishr informed us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, that a man of the people of Yemen called Tariq ibn al-Muraqqa' freed a slave of his as a sa'ibah. That slave of his died leaving wealth, and Tariq was brought it but refused to accept it. Ya'la ibn Umayyah, who was over Yemen at that time, wrote to Umar ibn al-Khattab about that, and Umar wrote to him: Hand over to the man the wealth of his freedman; if he accepts it, that is it, otherwise buy slaves with it and free them on his behalf. When the letter came, he called the man and offered him his freedman's wealth; he refused to accept it, so he bought with it sixteen or seventeen slaves and freed them."
"1401","224 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mansur informed us that Umar and Ibn Mas'ud said about the inheritance of the sa'ibah: It belongs to the one who freed him."
"1402","225 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who freed his slave as a sa'ibah and he died; his inheritance was brought to Ibn Mas'ud and he asked him about it. He said: You are most entitled to it, but he returned it to him and said to him: If you wish, place it for the same purpose for which you had designated it."
"1403","226 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to us that a woman of the settled folk, the settled folk of Muharib, freed a slave of hers and said: Go and affiliate with whomever you wish. The boy went and affiliated with Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar. The woman died, and her heirs disputed with Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar before Uthman ibn Affan. He called him and he informed him of the story, and he said to him: Go and affiliate with whomever you wish; so he returned to Abd al-Rahman and affiliated with him."
"1404","227 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, that he used to say: Any slave freed as a sa'ibah, his affair is in his own hand: he affiliates with whomever he wishes."
"1405","228 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam, from Rashid ibn Sa'd and Damrah ibn Habib who said: The clientage of the sa'ibah belongs to the one who freed him; he released his neck from slavery but did not release it from clientage."
"1406","Chapter: Those drowned, burned, etc. 229 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Sulayman al-A'mash informed us, from Ibrahim, from Umar, that he said about people who died together in one house with it unknown which of them died before his companion: Some of them inherit from others."
"1407","230 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim who said: A house in Syria fell upon a people and killed them, and Umar gave some of them inheritance from others."
"1408","231 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from Ali, that a people drowned in a ship, and Ali gave some of them inheritance from others."
"1409","232 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Sha'bi who said: The plague struck Syria in the year of Amwas, and the members of a household began dying to the last of them. That was written about to Umar, and Umar wrote: Give some of them inheritance from others."
"1410","233 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ash'ath ibn Sawwar informed us, he said: al-Sha'bi narrated that a ship sank with its people and it was unknown which of them died before his companion. They went to Ali and he said: Give each one of them inheritance from his companion."
"1411","234 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu al-Minhal who said: I heard Iyas ibn Abd al-Muzani being asked about a people upon whom a house fell and they died. He said: Some of them inherit from others."
"1412","235 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, from Mughirah who said: Qatan ibn Abdullah al-Dabbi informed me that a boy boarded with his mother on the Euphrates and they both drowned, and it was unknown which of them died before his companion. We went to Shurayh and he said: Give each one of them inheritance from his companion."
"1413","236 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim who said: Each one of them inherits from his companion, but neither of them inherits anything from what was inherited from his companion."
"1414","237 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: Some of them inherit from others."
"1415","238 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, that those slain at al-Yamamah, at Siffin, and at al-Harrah were not given inheritance from one another; their living agnates inherited them."
"1416","239 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ibn Shubrumah informed us, he said: A trustworthy one narrated to me, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, that he used to say: Each one of them is inherited by his (own) heirs."
"1417","240 - Sa'id said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, that Umm Kulthum bint Ali died together with her son Zayd ibn Umar; the two wailing parties met on the road, and it was unknown which of them died before his companion. She did not inherit from him nor did he inherit from her; and the people of Siffin did not inherit from one another, and the people of al-Harrah did not inherit from one another."
"1418","241 - Sa'id said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from his father, from Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit who said: It was said: Every group of mutual heirs whose order of death is obscure, in a collapse, drowning, burning, or any calamity - none of them inherits anything from another; they neither inherit nor are counted for exclusion; each one's living heirs inherit from him, as though there were no kinship between him and any of those who died with him."
"1419","242 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, concerning people who die together - drowned in a ship, or a house fell upon them, or they were killed - with it unknown which of them died before the other: some of them do not inherit from others unless it is known that he died before his companion; then the latter inherits from the former, and the latter is inherited by his agnate. If they do not know which of them died before his companion, some of them do not inherit from others; rather their living agnates inherit them."
"1420","243 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, Hakim ibn Umayr, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Awf who said: A dead person does not inherit from a dead person; only the living inherits the dead; their living agnates inherit them."
"1421","Chapter: A man gives charity and it returns to him by inheritance. 244 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Sayyar informed us, from al-Sha'bi, about a man who gives charity and the inheritance returns it to him. Al-Sha'bi said: Eat; Allah has not fed you anything unlawful."
"1422","245 - Sa'id said: Abu Awanah narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim who said: They used to like to direct it to the purpose to which they had directed it."
"1423","246 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Dawud or Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq who said: Eat whatever the shares of the Qur'an return to you."
"1424","247 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sha'bi who said: Whatever the Qur'an returns to you, eat."
"1425","248 - Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated, from Abdullah ibn Ata who said: Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated to me, from his father who said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I gave charity to my mother with a slave-girl, and my mother has died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have been rewarded, and it has returned to you in your inheritance. She said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has died owing fasting - would it suffice for her if I fast on her behalf? He said: Yes. [Flag: one word in the question is uncertain in print (my mother / indeed).]"
"1426","249 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, from Yunus, from Ibn Sirin, that a man gave charity to his mother with a slave-girl; his mother made a kitabah contract with her, then his mother died leaving her mukatabah. Imran ibn Husayn said to him: You inherit from your mother. He returned that to him and said: If you wish, place it for the same purpose for which you had designated it."
"1427","250 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, about a man who gives charity and then inherits it. He said: He saw no harm in it, but disliked that he buy it."
"1428","251 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr, Humayd al-A'raj, and Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, that Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Abd Rabbihi came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My garden is charity, for Allah and His Messenger. His parents came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We have no livelihood besides this. He returned it to them both, and then his parents died and he inherited it. Sufyan once said: and the two sons of Abu Bakr; Sa'id said: the two sons of Abu Bakr: Abdullah and Muhammad."
"1429","Chapter: The foundling-carried child (hamil) is not given inheritance except with proof. 252 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mujalid informed us, he said: al-Sha'bi narrated, he said: I took captive a woman on the day of Jalula, and with her was a boy; she used to say: My son. They were freed. The boy grew up, acquired wealth, then died. I was brought his inheritance and it was said: This is your son's inheritance. She said: He was not my son; I was only his wet-nurse, and he was the son of the dihqan (village chief) of the town. It was written to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and when the letter reached him he said: This does happen. He wrote to Shurayh: Do not give a carried child (of disputed parentage) inheritance except with proof."
"1430","253 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Jud'an, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote: Do not give a carried child (of disputed parentage) inheritance except with proof."
"1431","254 - Sa'id said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from al-A'mash, from his father Mihran, that Masruq gave him inheritance from a brother of his, though he was a hamil (carried child of disputed parentage)."
"1432","255 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, that they used to give the hamil inheritance."
"1433","256 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim who said: Every connected, known womb-tie is given inheritance."
"1434","257 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ubaydah informed us, from Ibrahim who said: Ibn Mas'ud said: If two men know one another in Islam and maintain ties, each one of them inherits from his companion."
"1435","258 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr who said: A man used to make a pact with a man, and each one of them would inherit from his companion. And Abu Bakr made a pact with a man and inherited from him."
"1436","259 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, from some of his companions, from al-Hasan who said: A man used to make a pact with a man in the pre-Islamic period, saying: You inherit from me and I inherit from you; he would get one-sixth of what he left, then the people of inheritance would divide their inheritances. It was abrogated by: And blood relatives are more entitled to one another."
"1437","260 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, about His Almighty statement: And for all We have made mawali - he said: Agnates; and those with whom your oaths have contracted - he said: Allies; so give them their share - of blood-money liability, support, and aid."
"1438","Chapter: A man manumits, dies leaving heirs, then the freedman dies. 261 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughirah informed us, he said: I asked Ibrahim about a man who freed a slave, died leaving his father and his son, then the freedman died. He said: His father gets one-sixth, and what remains goes to his son."
"1439","262 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: The entire inheritance goes to the son."
"1440","263 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to say that."
"1441","264 - Sa'id said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, about a man who died leaving his brother, his grandfather, and his freed client; then the freed client died. He said: The estate is between them in halves."
"1442","265 - Sa'id said: Abu Awanah narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, about two brothers who inherited a freed client whom their father had freed; then one of them died leaving a son. Shurayh said: Whoever owned something in his lifetime, it belongs to his heirs after his death. Ali, Abdullah, and Zayd said: Clientage belongs to the eldest (nearest)."
"1443","266 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from Shurayh, that he said: Whoever owned something in his lifetime, it belongs to his heirs after his death. Ali, Abdullah, and Zayd said: Clientage belongs to the eldest (nearest)."
"1444","267 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ash'ath ibn Sawwar informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Umar, Ali, Ibn Mas'ud, Abdullah, and Zayd used to assign clientage to the eldest (nearest)."
"1445","268 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh, that he used to say: Clientage is in the position of wealth."
"1446","269 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Shurayh used to assign clientage to the direct son of the manumitter and to his son's son."
"1447","270 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ubaydah informed us, he said: I asked Ibrahim about a man who died leaving a freed client and leaving three sons of his; then one of his sons died leaving a child, and the freed client died. He said: His inheritance goes to his two sons, and the son's son gets nothing. I said: Then one of the two sons died leaving a male child. He said: The estate goes to the other remaining one. I said: Then the other died, and all of them have children, some older than others. He said: Clientage is shared among them all."
"1448","271 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd informed us, from Ibn Sirin who said: When the freedman dies, the nearest of people to the one who freed him is considered, and his inheritance is assigned to him."
"1449","272 - Sa'id said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The freed client is a brother in religion and a blessing, and the most entitled of people to his inheritance is the nearest of them to the manumitter."
"1450","273 - Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Sulayman ibn Yasar who said: Ali and al-Zubayr disputed about the freed clients of Safiyyah. Ali said: I pay blood-money on their behalf and I inherit from them. Al-Zubayr said: They are the freed clients of my mother and I inherit from them. Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf called out to them: You do not know which of you will die sooner; so they fell silent."
"1451","274 - Saeed said: Abu Muawiyah narrated, he said: Ubaydah al-Dabbi narrated, from Ibrahim, he said: Ali and al-Zubayr disputed before Umar about a freed slave of Safiyyah. Ali said: He is the freed slave of my paternal aunt and I bear his blood-money liability, and al-Zubayr said: He is the freed slave of my mother and I inherit from him. So Umar ruled the inheritance for al-Zubayr and ruled the liability against Ali. Ibrahim said: So the wala belongs to the family of al-Zubayr as long as they have descendants. I said: What is descendants? He said: Male children; if there is no male child, the wala returns to Ali."
"1452","275 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: al-Shaybani informed us, from al-Shaabi, he said: He ruled the wala of the freed slaves of Safiyyah for al-Zubayr rather than al-Abbas, and he ruled the wala of the freed slaves of Umm Hani for Jadah ibn Hubayrah rather than Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1453","Chapter on the prohibition of selling wala and gifting it. 276 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling wala and gifting it."
"1454","277 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: Ali said: Wala is like an alliance pact; it is not sold and not gifted. Leave it where Allah placed it."
"1455","278 - Saeed said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: Wala is only like lineage; would a man sell his lineage?"
"1456","279 - Saeed said: Abu Awanah narrated, from Amr ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wala belongs to the one who emancipates."
"1457","280 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, that Maymunah gifted the wala of Sulayman ibn Yasar to Ibn Abbas, and he was a mukatab (a slave under a manumission contract)."
"1458","281 - Saeed said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Inheritance is for the paternal male relatives; if there is no paternal male relative, then the wala."
"1459","282 - Saeed said: Jarir narrated, from Mansur, he said: I asked Ibrahim about a man who freed a slave for the sake of Allah, then the freed man went and took another man as his patron. He said: He has no right to do that except if the emancipator gifts it."
"1460","283 - Saeed said: Abu Muawiyah narrated, he said: Abu Asim al-Thaqafi narrated, from al-Shaabi, from Shurayh, that he used to treat wala like inheritance."
"1461","284 - Saeed said: Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated, from Dawud, from Saeed ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Wala is a bond like lineage; it is not sold and not gifted."
"1462","Chapter on one who cuts off an inheritance which Allah ordained. 285 - Saeed said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Kinani, from Sulayman ibn Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cuts off an inheritance which Allah ordained, Allah will cut off his inheritance from Paradise."
"1463","286 - Saeed said: Nafi ibn Fadalah narrated, from al-Nadr ibn Shufayy, from Imran ibn Sulaym, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cuts off an inheritance which Allah ordained, Allah will cut off his inheritance in Paradise."
"1464","287 - Saeed said: Abu Muawiyah narrated, he said: al-Amash narrated, from Muslim ibn Subayh, he said: Masruq was asked: Did Aishah know the inheritance laws well? He said: I saw the senior Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking her about the inheritance laws."
"1465","288 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Attach the wealth to the fixed shares; whatever the fixed shares leave is for the closest male, or he said: for the closest male relative."
"1466","289 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Attach the wealth to the fixed shares; if the fixed shares leave anything, it is for the closest male womb-relative."
"1467","290 - Saeed said: Abu Muawiyah narrated, he said: al-Amash narrated, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Umar was asked about an inheritance case and could not answer it well, then was asked about another case and could not answer it well, so he said: There is no harm."
"1468","291 - Saeed narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr, from Abu Salih, that Sad ibn Ubadah divided wealth among his children and left for Syria; a son was born to him afterwards, then he died. Abu Bakr and Umar came to Qays ibn Sad and said: Sad divided among his children not knowing what would happen, and we think you should return a share to this boy. Qays said: I will not return anything Sad did, but my own share is for him."
"1469","292 - Saeed said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, that Sad ibn Ubadah divided his wealth among his children, leaving an unborn child unknown, and died. Abu Bakr and Umar went to Qays ibn Sad and said to him, and he said: As for what Sad did I will not change, but I call you to witness that my share is for him. He said: I said to Ata: Did he divide for him according to the Book of Allah? He said: We only knew them dividing according to the Book of Allah."
"1470","293 - Saeed said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, he said: al-Awzai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Treat your children equally in gifts; had I favored anyone I would have favored women over men."
"1471","294 - Saeed said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Saeed ibn Yusuf, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this hadith."
"1472","Chapter on the wife inheriting from her husband's blood-money. 295 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, he said: al-Zuhri narrated, having heard Saeed ibn al-Musayyab say: The blood-money is for the paternal relatives liable for it, and the wife inherits nothing from her husband's blood-money. Al-Dahhak al-Kilabi said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to me instructing me to give the wife of Ashyam al-Dababi a share of her husband Ashyam's blood-money."
"1473","296 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: If I did not hear it from al-Zuhri, then Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Saeed ibn al-Musayyab, that a woman came to Umar ibn al-Khattab whose husband had been killed and asked to be given a share of his blood-money. He said: I know of nothing for you. Then he asked the people who had any knowledge from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi stood and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to me instructing me to give the wife of Ashyam a share of her husband Ashyam's blood-money. So Umar ibn al-Khattab gave her a share."
"1474","297 - Saeed said: Abu Qudamah narrated, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Saeed ibn al-Musayyab, he said: A woman came to Umar and said she was given nothing from her husband's blood-money. He said: I consider the blood-money only for the paternal kin, for they bear his liability. Does any of you have anything conveyed from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi stood and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to me about the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi instructing me to give her a share of her husband's blood-money. So Umar gave her a share."
"1475","298 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from Umar ibn Saeed ibn Masruq, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, that he heard al-Shaabi say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a husband a share of blood-money."
"1476","299 - Saeed said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, he said: al-Amash informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood-money follows the inheritance, and the liability payment is upon the paternal kin."
"1477","300 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he was asked about a wife: does she inherit from her husband's blood-money? Ibrahim said: The blood-money is divided according to Allah's fixed shares."
"1478","301 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani informed us, he said: I said to al-Shaabi: Do maternal siblings inherit anything from the blood-money? He said: As for you, you have looked at the Quran; every heir inherits from the blood-money."
"1479","302 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ashath ibn Sawwar informed us, he said: al-Shaabi informed us, from one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The blood-money is divided according to Allah's fixed shares."
"1480","303 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, having heard Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ali say: Ali ibn Abi Talib said: He has wronged who deprives maternal siblings of their share of the blood-money."
"1481","304 - Saeed said: Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn say: Ali said: He has wronged who deprives maternal siblings of their share of the blood-money."
"1482","305 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Shaabi, that Ali would not give maternal siblings any share of the blood-money."
"1483","306 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, from Ali, that he used to say: Maternal siblings, the husband, and the wife inherit nothing from the blood-money."
"1484","307 - Saeed said: Khalid narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: Every heir inherits from the blood-money except the husband and the wife, apart from others entitled without blood-money [Flag: report wording compressed; literal sense: every heir inherits from the blood-money except the husband and wife]."
"1485","308 - Saeed said: Abu Muawiyah narrated, he said: Layth narrated, from Abu Amr al-Abdi, from Ali, he said: Divide the blood-money as you divide the inheritance."
"1486","Inheritance of the apostate. 309 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Musa ibn Abi Kathir informed us, he said: I asked Saeed ibn al-Musayyab about the waiting period of an apostate's wife. He said: Three menstrual cycles. I said: If he is killed? He said: Then four months and ten days. I said: And his inheritance? He said: We inherit from them and they do not inherit from us."
"1487","310 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: The apostate's inheritance belongs to his heirs."
"1488","311 - Saeed said: Abu Muawiyah narrated, he said: al-Amash narrated, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, he said: Ali was brought al-Mustawrid al-Ijli who had apostatized from Islam; he offered him Islam and he refused, so he struck his neck and gave his inheritance to his Muslim heirs. Saeed said: No one has this hadith except Abu Muawiyah."
"1489","312 - Saeed said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Mamar, from a man of the Jazirah, he said: I wrote to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz about a captive who became Christian in Byzantine land. He wrote: If that is established by proof, divide his wealth among his heirs."
"1490","313 - Saeed said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Mamar, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, about a man who becomes Christian in Byzantine land, he said: His wife observes a waiting period of three menstrual cycles."
"1491","Chapter on acknowledgment and denial. 314 - Saeed said: Abu Awanah narrated, from Mutarrif, from Amir al-Shaabi, about three men who inherited three hundred dirhams, then one of them acknowledged a debt of one hundred. He said: He is given a third of the hundred. Then he said: This is wrong; no inheritance is inherited until the debt is settled, so he ordered him to pay the hundred."
"1492","315 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mutarrif informed us, from al-Shaabi, he said: If an heir acknowledges a debt, it is upon him in his share of his portion; then he said afterwards: It is taken out of all his portion."
"1493","316 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, about a man who died and a man claimed a debt against him, acknowledged by some of the heirs: if one of them acknowledges, it is upon him in his share of his portion; if two men, or one man and two women, acknowledge, it is binding on all of them."
"1494","317 - Saeed said: Khalid narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, about a man who claimed a thousand dirhams against a deceased man who left two sons and two thousand dirhams; one acknowledged and the other refused. He said: The one who acknowledged gives five hundred dirhams."
"1495","318 - Saeed said: Abu Awanah narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: If some of the heirs claim a brother or sister, it is nothing until they all acknowledge."
"1496","319 - Saeed said: Abu Shihab narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ibn Sirin, from Shurayh, he said: Whoever acknowledges a debt to an heir at death, it is not valid."
"1497","320 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Shurayh, that he would not allow a man's acknowledgment at death of a debt to an heir."
"1498","321 - Saeed said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated, from Mughirah, from al-Shaabi, he said: If two witnesses, or one man and two women, from among the heirs testify to a debt against the deceased, it is binding on all the heirs."
"1499","322 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Sayyar informed us, he said: Hammad reported from Ibrahim, and he said: If some of the heirs testify to a debt against the deceased, it is in their shares, or they pursue the rest of the heirs with it."
"1500","323 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus and Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: If a man acknowledges his wife's dowry at death, she is entitled to a dowry like hers."
"1501","324 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, that he said the same as al-Hasan's saying."
"1502","325 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: A shaykh of Kufah informed us, from al-Shaabi, that he used to say: His acknowledgment to her at death is not valid unless his acknowledgment was in health before illness, because she is an heir and no bequest to an heir is valid. Hushaym said: And that is the opinion. End of the Book of Inheritance Laws."
"1503","Book of Bequests. 326 - Saeed ibn Mansur informed us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: They used to write at the beginning of their wills: This is what so-and-so son of so-and-so bequeathed; he bequeathed testifying that there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that the Hour is coming without doubt, and that Allah will resurrect those in the graves. And he bequeathed to those of his family he leaves to fear Allah, make peace among themselves, and obey Allah and His Messenger if they are believers. And he bequeathed to them what Ibrahim enjoined upon his sons, and Yaqub: O my sons, Allah has chosen the religion for you, so do not die except as Muslims."
"1504","327 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: He said: Sayyar Abu al-Hakam informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he said: al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym bequeathed: This is what al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym bequeathed, calling Allah to witness over himself, and Allah suffices as witness, requiter of His righteous servants and rewarder: that I am pleased with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Prophet. And I am pleased for myself and those who obey me to worship Allah among the worshippers, praise Him among those who praise, and give sincere counsel to the Muslim community."
"1505","328 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Abu Bishr dictated his will to me, saying: Write: This is what Jafar ibn Iyas bequeathed; he bequeathed testifying that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that the Hour is coming without doubt, and that Allah will resurrect those in the graves. I am pleased with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Prophet; upon that I live, upon it I die, and upon it I shall be resurrected. And he bequeathed to his family and those he leaves after him to fear Allah as He should be feared and not die except as Muslims."
"1506","329 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, he said: He said: I heard this hadith from Silah ibn Zufar seventy years ago. He said: A man came to Abdullah on a piebald horse or mule and said: Do you command me to buy this? He said: What is the matter with it? He said: A man appointed me executor and it is from his estate; I brought it to market and the price stood. He said: Do not buy anything from his estate, nor borrow from it."
"1507","Chapter: may a man bequeath more than a third of his wealth? 330 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, he said: al-Zuhri narrated, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, that he arrived in Makkah in the year of the Conquest. He said: I fell ill with an illness in which I feared death for myself, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came visiting me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I leave much wealth and leave no heir except my daughter; shall I give two-thirds of my wealth in charity? He said: No. He said: Half? He said: No. He said: A third? He said: A third, and a third is much. If you leave your heirs rich it is better than leaving them dependent begging people. You will never spend an expense - I think he said - seeking Allah's Face thereby, but you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you raise to your wife's mouth. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will I be left behind from my emigration? He said: You will not be left behind after me doing a deed seeking Allah's Face but you will increase in rank and degree thereby; perhaps you will be left so that some peoples benefit by you and others are harmed by you. O Allah, complete my Companions' emigration and do not turn them back on their heels. But the wretched Sad ibn Khawlah, to whom sympathy for dying in Makkah."
"1508","331 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ibn Awn informed us, from Amr ibn Saeed, he said: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari narrated to me, he said: Three men from Sad's children informed me, this being one of them, meaning Amir ibn Sad, that Sad fell ill in Makkah and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came visiting him. Sad said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I leave wealth and have no heir except distant kindred; shall I bequeath all my wealth? He said: No. He said: Half of it? He said: No. He said: A third of it? He said: A third, and a third is much. If you leave your family in comfort - or he said: in good - it is better than leaving them begging people."
"1509","332 - Saeed said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, he said: Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Sad ibn Malik, he said: I fell ill and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me and said to me: Have you made a will? I said: Yes, I bequeathed all my wealth to the poor and in Allah's path. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Bequeath a tenth. I said: O Messenger of Allah, my wealth is much and my heirs are rich. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept reducing with me and I with him until he said: Bequeath a third, and a third is much."
"1510","333 - Saeed said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, he said: Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, he said: None of us would reach a third in his will without reducing something from it, because of the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A third, and a third is much."
"1511","334 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Juwaybir informed us, from al-Dahhak, that Abu Bakr and Ali bequeathed a fifth of their wealth to non-inheriting relatives."
"1512","335 - Saeed said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, he said: Ishaq ibn Suwayd informed us, he said: al-Ala ibn Ziyad narrated, he said: An old man came to Umar and said: O Commander of the Faithful, I am an old man with much wealth, and Bedouin freedmen, distant kindred of remote lineage, will inherit from me; shall I bequeath all my wealth? He said: No. He said: O Commander of the Faithful, I am an old man with much wealth and Bedouin freedmen, distant kindred of remote lineage, will inherit from me; shall I bequeath all my wealth? He said: No. He kept lowering him until he reached a tenth."
"1513","336 - Saeed said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, he said: I heard Ishaq ibn Suwayd narrating from al-Ala ibn Ziyad, he said: My father commanded me to ask the scholars of Basrah: which bequest is best? Whatever they agree upon is my will. So I asked them and they agreed upon a fifth."
"1514","337 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: A fifth in bequest was dearer to them than a fourth, and a fourth dearer to them than a third. And it was said: The two bitterest matters are withholding in life and squandering at death."
"1515","338 - Saeed said: Abu Muawiyah narrated, he said: al-Amash narrated, from Abdullah ibn Sinan al-Asadi, he said: Ibn Masud said: Those two are the bitterest: withholding in life and squandering at death."
"1516","339 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Sinan al-Asadi, he said: Ibn Masud said: Stinginess in life and squandering at death, those two are the bitterest of matters."
"1517","340 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Shaabi: A fifth was dearer to them than a third; as for a third, it is the limit of the overstepper."
"1518","341 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: Shurayh said: A third is an exertion, and it is permissible."
"1519","342 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Dawud informed us, from Ikrimah, he said: Deviation in bequest and causing harm in it are among the major sins."
"1520","343 - Saeed said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Deviation in bequest and causing harm in it are among the major sins."
"1521","344 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from Dawud, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Injustice, deviation, and causing harm in bequest are among the major sins."
"1522","345 - Saeed said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, he said: Dawud informed us, from Amir, he said: Whoever bequeaths a bequest without exceeding the limit and without injustice gets a reward like what he gave, while he is healthy."
"1523","346 - Saeed said: Khalid and Hushaym narrated, both saying: Dawud informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Umar - and Hushaym said: Ibn Amr - from Thumamah ibn Hazn, he said: He said to me: Did your father bequeath? I said: No. He said: Then order him to bequeath, for it has reached us that it completes what is deficient of zakat."
"1524","347 - Saeed said: Khalid narrated, he said: Ubaydah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he disliked a man bequeathing a third or a quarter, saying: the sieve and the like enter into that."
"1525","348 - Saeed said: Hushaym and Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, both saying: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he disliked a man bequeathing like the share of one of the heirs, even if less than a third."
"1526","349 - Saeed said: Khalid narrated, he said: Dawud informed us, from Amir, about a man with three sons who bequeaths to a man like the share of one of his children. He said: He is made a fourth."
"1527","350 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Awf informed us, he said: I witnessed Hisham ibn Hubayrah brought a case of a man who bequeathed to a man like the share of one of his children. Hisham said: If his children are male, he gets a male's share; if they are female, he gets the female's share."
"1528","351 - Saeed said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated, he said: al-Amash narrated, from Ibrahim, he said: If a man bequeaths a third, a fourth, or a fifth of his wealth, it is from his present and future wealth. If he bequeaths to so-and-so such-and-such, and to so-and-so such-and-such, it is from his present wealth until it reaches a third; when it reaches a third, it is from the present and the future."
"1529","352 - Saeed said: Abu Muawiyah narrated, he said: al-Amash narrated, from Ibrahim, he said: If a man bequeaths a third or a fourth, it is in tangible wealth and debt owed to him. If he bequeaths thirty or forty dirhams, it is from tangible wealth, not debt."
"1530","353 - Saeed said: Jarir narrated, from al-Amash and Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: If a man bequeaths a third or a fourth, the bequest is upon the present and the future. If he bequeaths named dirhams, a garment, or an animal, the bequest is in the present wealth up to a third."
"1531","354 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Abdullah ibn Mamar said: Whoever says: put my third where Allah commanded, we put it for non-inheriting kin. Whoever names something, we put it where he named."
"1532","355 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus and Humayd informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: Whoever bequeaths to non-kin, those bequeathed to get a third of the third, and his kin get two-thirds of the third."
"1533","356 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, he said: Whoever dies without bequeathing to his kin has sealed his deed with disobedience."
"1534","357 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Juwaybir informed us, from al-Dahhak, that he used to say: Had I been a ruler and been brought one who bequeathed to other than his kin, I would reject that even if houses were built with it or wealth taken with it."
"1535","358 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that he used to say: Bequest was before inheritance; when inheritance was revealed, inheritance abrogated those who inherit, and bequest remained for those who do not inherit, so it stands. Whoever bequeaths to other than kin, his bequest is not valid, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No bequest to an heir."
"1536","359 - Saeed said: Abu Attab Muslim ibn Ata al-Qurashi informed us that a man died bequeathing something among his kin, and the kin deemed it little. They said to me: Would you increase them, and I was the executor. I said: I cannot increase them beyond what was ordered for them. They said: Will you ask al-Hasan? I said: Yes. So I went with Humayd al-Tawil to al-Hasan, and Humayd asked him about that while I listened. He said: I see he named something for them; stop at what he named for them."
"1537","360 - Saeed said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, he said: al-Amash narrated, from Muslim ibn Subayh, he said: A neighbor of Masruq bequeathed and called him to witness; he found him squandering and being excessive. Masruq said: Allah divided among you and apportioned well; whoever prefers his own opinion over Allah's opinion strays. Bequeath to your kin who do not inherit, leave wealth upon Allah's division, and he refused to witness."
"1538","361 - Saeed said: Abu Muawiyah narrated, he said: al-Amash narrated, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, he said: He attended a man bequeathing who bequeathed improper things. Masruq said to him: Allah divided among you and apportioned well; whoever prefers his opinion over Allah's opinion strays. Bequeath to your kin who do not inherit you, then leave wealth as Allah divided it."
"1539","362 - Saeed said: Abu Shihab narrated, from al-Amash, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, about a man who gifted his children favoring some over others. He said to him: Allah divided among you and apportioned well; whoever prefers his opinion over Allah's opinion strays. Bequeath to your kin who do not inherit you, and leave wealth as Allah divided it."
"1540","363 - Saeed said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Yaqub ibn al-Qaqa, from Ata and Muhammad ibn Suhayb, from Ikrimah, about a man who bequeaths a share of his wealth. He said: No, it is nothing; he did not specify. Al-Hasan said: He gets a sixth in every case."
"1541","364 - Saeed said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, he said: Zaidah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Yasar ibn Abi Karib informed us that a man came to Shurayh asking about it. He said: The fixed shares are reckoned; whatever the shares reach, the beneficiary is given a share like one of them."
"1542","365 - Saeed said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Yaqub ibn al-Qaqa, from Ata, and from Matar, from al-Hasan, about a man who bequeaths to the sons of so-and-so. He said: Male and female are equal, unless he says: for the male like the share of two females."
"1543","366 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: If a man bequeaths his third to the sons of so-and-so, it is theirs, male and female equal therein."
"1544","Chapter on a man bequeathing to a man, then the beneficiary dies. 367 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mansur and Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, about a man who bequeaths a bequest to a man, then the beneficiary dies before the testator. He said: The bequest is for the beneficiary's child. Saeed said: He did nothing of value."
"1545","368 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: It returns to the testator's heirs. Saeed said: He was right."
"1546","369 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, about a man who bequeaths a third of his wealth then acquires wealth before dying, by inheritance or otherwise. He said: The one he bequeathed to gets a third of his wealth and a third of what he acquired."
"1547","370 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: If a man makes a bequest then makes another bequest, his later bequest of the two stands."
"1548","371 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, Abu al-Shatha, and Ata, they said: The last bequest is followed."
"1549","372 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham, freedman of Quraysh, narrated: I read the will of Hafsah, Mother of the Believers; in it she had bequeathed things, and at the end of her will was: if my dependents (?) come (?) so long as I have not changed it [Flag: wording garbled/truncated in source]."
"1550","373 - Saeed said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi, he said: Aishah, Mother of the Believers, said: A man writes in his will: if death befalls me before I change this will of mine."
"1551","374 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: If a man makes a bequest in his illness then recovers and does not change that will of his until he dies afterwards, what is in his will is valid."
"1552","375 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, about a man who bequeaths in his illness: if an event befalls me - intending that in his illness - his slave is free; then he recovers. He said: If he wishes, he may sell him."
"1553","376 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: al-Shaybani informed us, from al-Shaabi, he said: A man may revoke all his will except manumission."
"1554","377 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Hisham informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that he used to say that also."
"1555","378 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to command bequest to one's kin. It was said to him: Even if they are rich? He said: Their richness does not bar them from the right Allah gave them."
"1556","379 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, he said: Whoever dies without bequeathing to his kin has sealed his deed with disobedience."
"1557","380 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Juwaybir informed us, from al-Dahhak, he said: Had I been a ruler and been brought a man who bequeathed to other than his kin, I would reject that even if houses were built with it and wealth taken with it."
"1558","381 - Saeed said: Abu Muawiyah narrated, he said: Abu Asim al-Thaqafi narrated, he said: Ibrahim al-Nakhai said to me: What do you say about a man who bequeaths half his wealth, a third of his wealth, and a fourth of his wealth? I said: It is not valid. He said: But they allowed it. I said: I do not know. He said: Hold twelve; take out half of it, six, a third of it, four, and a fourth of it, three. Then divide the wealth over thirteen: the owner of the half gets six, the owner of the third four, and the owner of the fourth three."
"1559","Chapter on the bequest of the traveler and the pregnant woman. 382 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughirah informed us, from al-Shaabi, he said: If a man gives a gift when he puts his foot in the stirrup for travel, it is a bequest from the third."
"1560","383 - Saeed said: Jarir narrated, from Mughirah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: His bequest is valid and is not from the third."
"1561","384 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, about the traveler: whatever he does of things is from the whole wealth. Hushaym said: And that is the opinion."
"1562","385 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, from Jabir, from al-Shaabi, from Shurayh, he said: Whatever the pregnant woman does of things is from the third."
"1563","386 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, he said: Iyas ibn Muawiyah sent me when he was seized on suspicion. He said: Go to al-Hasan and ask him about my state regarding what I dispose of in my wealth: is it from the third or from the whole wealth? So I came to al-Hasan and mentioned that to him. He said: What he disposes of in his state is from the third; he is like the sick."
"1564","387 - Saeed said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yahya ibn Saeed, that he heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad say: Whatever the pregnant woman gives, a third of it is for her husband or for one of those who inherit her apart from the third, when it is not from her share or from his share - the shaykh doubted [Flag: reporter expresses doubt about wording]."
"1565","Chapter on a man seeking his heirs' permission to bequeath more than a third. 388 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, he said: al-Shaabi narrated, from Shurayh, that he said about a man who sought his heirs' permission and they allowed him to bequeath more than a third, and he did; then when he died they refused to allow his bequest. Shurayh said: People may feel shy of their companion while he is alive among them; when they shake their hands of dust, they have the choice: if they wish they allow, if they wish they reject."
"1566","389 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ubaydah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: And I was informed from Mansur, from Ibrahim, that he used to say that."
"1567","390 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: al-Masudi informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Thaqafi, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman - al-Masudi said: and I think I heard it from al-Qasim - he said: Abdullah said: That is unwillingness; it is not valid."
"1568","391 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ayyub Abu al-Ala informed us, he said: I heard al-Hakam ibn Utaybah narrate from Ibn Masud the same."
"1569","392 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: If they allowed him, they may not retract after his death."
"1570","393 - Saeed said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, the same."
"1571","Chapter on a man bequeathing manumission and other things. 394 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ashath ibn Sawwar informed us, he said: Nafi narrated, from Ibn Umar, that he used to say about a bequest when it falls short of the third: begin with manumission."
"1572","395 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: al-Shaybani informed us, from Masruq ibn al-Ajda, he said: Begin with manumission."
"1573","396 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ashath informed us, from Shurayh, that he used to say: Begin with manumission. He said: And al-Hakam ibn Utaybah narrated to us from Shurayh that he judged so among people of Kindah, beginning with manumission."
"1574","397 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, from Mughirah and Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, he said: Begin with manumission."
"1575","398 - Saeed said: Jarir narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, about a man who bequeaths manumission and other things. He said: Begin with manumission before the bequest; if manumission takes up the third, the bequest-holders get nothing. If manumission exceeds the third, he works for the remainder and is freed. If manumission is less than the third, begin with manumission, and what remains of the third is among the bequest-holders by their shares."
"1576","399 - Saeed said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydillah, from al-Shaabi, from Shurayh, the same."
"1577","400 - Saeed said: Jarir narrated, from Mughirah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: Begin with manumission only when it is a slave owned by him whom he named by name; that is what is begun with. If he says: free a slave on my behalf, the slave and the rest of the bequest are equal."
"1578","401 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ashath ibn Sawwar informed us, from al-Shaabi, that he used to say: If he frees in his will a slave owned by him and his will falls short, begin with him. If he says: free on my behalf, then by shares."
"1579","402 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mutarrif reported, from Ibrahim, he said: Begin with manumission. And al-Shaabi said: Begin with shares."
"1580","403 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Khalid and Yunus informed us, from Ibn Sirin, he said: By shares."
"1581","404 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: By shares."
"1582","405 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he said: Begin with manumission; then he said afterwards: By shares."
"1583","Chapter on a man who frees at death owning no wealth besides him. 406 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Hajjaj informed us, from al-Ala ibn Badr, from Abu Yahya al-Makki, that a man freed a slave of his at death, owning no wealth besides him, with a debt upon him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that he work for his value."
"1584","407 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from a man of Banu Udhrah, that a man of them freed a slave of his at death, having no wealth besides him. That was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he freed a third of him and made him work for two-thirds."
"1585","408 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man of the Ansar freed six slaves of his at death, having no wealth besides them. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he was angered by that and said: I intended not to pray over him. Then he called his slaves, divided them into three parts, cast lots among them, freed two and kept four enslaved."
"1586","409 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Khalid informed us, he said: Abu Qilabah narrated, from Abu Zayd al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"1587","410 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ibn Awn informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"1588","411 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Makhul, from Saeed ibn al-Musayyab, that a man freed six slaves of his in his illness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and kept four enslaved."
"1589","412 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: They work; a third of them is freed and they work for two-thirds."
"1590","413 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Shaabi, with the same as Ibrahim's saying."
"1591","414 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mutarrif informed us, from al-Shaabi, that he heard him say the same as Ibrahim said."
"1592","415 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say the same as Ibrahim and al-Shaabi said when he has no debt upon him. If he has a debt greater than his value, he is a slave and is sold; unless the debt is less than his value by one dirham or more, then when it is so, working applies."
"1593","416 - Saeed said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, and Mutarrif, from al-Shaabi, about a man who frees his slave at death, having no wealth besides him, with a debt equal to his value - or he said: more - they said: He works for his value."
"1594","Chapter: does the living fulfill a vow for the dead? 417 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that Sad ibn Ubadah sought the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruling about a vow upon his mother who died before fulfilling it. He said: Fulfill it on her behalf."
"1595","418 - Saeed said: Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, he said: Sad ibn Ubadah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mother died without making a will; will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes."
"1596","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur and Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah said: O Messenger of Allah, I was the son of Umm Sa'd, and she has died, so will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: ""Yes."" He said: Then which charity is best? He said: ""Giving water to drink."" He said: So he made two cisterns in Madinah. Al-Hasan said: And I would sometimes run between them while I was a boy."
"1597","Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mother died and did not make a bequest; shall I make a bequest on her behalf? He said: ""Yes."""
"1598","Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father: ""There is no man who dies when bequest is enjoined upon him and he does not make a bequest, except that his family are duty-bound to make a bequest on his behalf."""
"1599","Sa'id said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, he said: Tawus was asked about the charity of the living on behalf of the dead; he said: Excellent, and it pleased him."
"1600","Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, that he asked Ibn 'Abbas about a vow of i'tikaf that was upon his mother, and she died. He said: ""Fast on her behalf and perform i'tikaf on her behalf."""
"1601","Sa'id said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from 'Amir ibn Mus'ab, that 'A'ishah performed i'tikaf on behalf of her brother 'Abd al-Rahman after he died."
"1602","Chapter: There is no bequest for an heir. Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Mujahid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a caller, who announced: ""There is no bequest for an heir, and no gift by a woman is permissible except with her husband's permission, and the child belongs to the bed."""
"1603","Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No bequest for an heir is permissible unless the heirs approve it."""
"1604","Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Shurahbil ibn Muslim al-Khawlani narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in his sermon in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage: ""Indeed Allah has given every possessor of a right his right, so there is no bequest for an heir. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone, and their reckoning is upon Allah. Whoever claims descent from other than his father or attaches himself to other than his masters, upon him is the continuous curse of Allah until the Day of Resurrection; no obligatory nor voluntary deed will be accepted from him. No woman should spend anything from her house except with her husband's permission."" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, not even food? He said: ""That is the best of our wealth."" Then he said: ""The borrowed item must be returned, the granted milch animal must be returned, the debt must be paid, and the guarantor is liable."""
"1605","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Talhah Abu Muhammad, the freedman of Bahilah, informed us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from 'Amr ibn Kharijah al-Ash'ari, he said: I attended the pilgrimage with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I was between the forelegs(?) of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while she was grinding her cud, and her saliva was flowing between my shoulders. He said: So I heard him say: ""Indeed Allah has given every possessor of a right his right, and no bequest for an heir is permissible. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Whoever claims descent from other than his father or attaches himself to other than his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; no obligatory nor voluntary deed will be accepted from him."""
"1606","Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No bequest for an heir is permissible."""
"1607","Chapter of the bequest of the minor. Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr and Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm, from 'Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, that a boy from Ghassan fell ill, and 'Umar was informed of it, and he said: Order him to make a bequest. So he bequeathed the well of Jusham, which was sold for thirty thousand, while he was ten years old, or twelve years old."
"1608","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, that a boy from the Ansar bequeathed to maternal uncles of his from Ghassan a land called the well of Jusham, which was valued at thirty thousand, and that was raised to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he approved the bequest. Yahya said: And the boy was ten years old."
"1609","Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: The bequest of a young slave-girl, which they deemed small and insignificant, was raised to 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, and 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah said: ""Whoever hits the truth, we approve it."""
"1610","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus and Hisham informed us, from Ibn Sirin, he said: The bequest of a young slave-girl, which they deemed small and insignificant, was raised to 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, and 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah said: ""Whoever hits the truth, we approve his bequest."""
"1611","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: The bequest of a boy who had not yet reached puberty was raised to Shurayh, and Shurayh said: ""Whoever hits the truth, we approve his bequest."""
"1612","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: ""The divorce of a boy is not valid until he reaches puberty, or his peers reach puberty, nor his manumission, nor his bequest, nor his gift, nor his charity."""
"1613","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, the same except divorce."
"1614","Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Ikrimah, that Safiyyah bint Huyayy sold her chamber to Mu'awiyah for one hundred thousand, and she had a Jewish brother, so she offered him to accept Islam so that he would inherit, but he refused, so she bequeathed him a third of the hundred thousand."
"1615","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from al-Hasan, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab bequeathed four thousand to the mothers of his children."
"1616","Chapter concerning the mudabbar (a slave promised freedom upon his master's death). Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, he heard Jabir ibn 'Abdullah say: A man from the Ansar made tadbir of a slave boy of his, and he had no wealth besides him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold him, and Ibn al-Nahham bought him. Jabir said: A Coptic slave who died in the first year during the rule of Ibn al-Zubayr."
"1617","Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, similar to it, he said: And his name was Ya'qub the Copt."
"1618","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Malik informed us, from 'Ata, that a man freed a slave boy of his with posthumous effect, and he had no wealth besides him, and that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he became angry at that, and he called the boy and sold him for seven hundred dirhams, then he handed the price to him and said: ""Spend it."""
"1619","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from 'Ata, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of 'Abd al-Malik."
"1620","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman informed us, from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold the service of the mudabbar."
"1621","Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, that he disliked the sale of one freed with posthumous effect except from himself (i.e. selling his own service to himself)."
"1622","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that he disliked selling him, but permitted selling his service."
"1623","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that he used to say concerning one freed with posthumous effect: ""Do not sell him and do not give him as a gift."""
"1624","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Husayn informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he disliked selling him."
"1625","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say concerning one freed with posthumous effect: ""He is not to be sold."" It was said to him: What if his owner is in need and has nothing besides him? They kept pressing him until he permitted them, though his opinion was that he should not be sold."
"1626","Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: ""The mudabbara (female slave promised freedom upon her master's death) is not to be sold, nor given as dowry, nor given as a gift, and her master may have intercourse with her if he wishes, and her child has the same status as her."""
"1627","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Qays ibn Ka'b ibn al-Ahnaf al-Nakha'i narrated to me, from his grandfather, that a man freed a slave boy of his with posthumous effect, and when his master's life grew long, he contracted him to buy his service for known installments; so he paid some and some remained, then his master died, and his heirs disputed with him before 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, and he said: ""As for what your master took during his life, it is his, and as for what remains, you owe nothing when your master has died."""
"1628","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj informed us, he said: Dawud ibn Hurayth al-Asadi informed me that he witnessed Shurayh judge likewise."
"1629","Sa'id said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, he said: ""If he sells the service of the mudabbar to himself (i.e. the slave buys his own service), then he (the master) dies while something remains due from him, he is free and owes nothing."""
"1630","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: It was narrated to me from Ibrahim, that he used to say: ""They (the heirs) may take him for what remains."""
"1631","Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: ""The mudabbar is a bequest; his owner may revoke it whenever he wishes."""
"1632","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that he said: ""The child of the woman freed with posthumous effect has the same status as her."""
"1633","Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, the same."
"1634","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Husayn informed us, from al-Sha'bi, the same."
"1635","Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu al-Sha'tha, he said: ""The children of the mudabbara are slaves."""
"1636","Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Ubaydullah, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Abdullah, and from Shurayh, that they both said: ""The children of the umm walad and the mudabbara"" — they said: ""they are enslaved with their enslavement, and freed with their freeing."""
"1637","Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, concerning a man who marries off his umm walad and she bears children, he said: ""When their mother is freed, they are free."""
"1638","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Uthman ibn Hakim informed us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Zayd ibn Thabit permitted selling the child of the woman freed with posthumous effect, and said: ""Let him take from her womb what he can."""
"1639","Sa'id said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Masruq said: ""The mudabbar is free of wealth (i.e. counts against the whole estate, not the third)."" And Shurayh said: ""He is from the third."""
"1640","Sa'id said: Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Qasim ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Masruq, he said: ""The mudabbar is from the entire wealth."""
"1641","Sa'id said: Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from 'Amir, from 'Abdullah, he said: ""From the entire wealth."""
"1642","Sa'id said: Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from 'Amir, from Shurayh, he said: ""He is from the third."""
"1643","Sa'id said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Shurayh, he said: ""From the third."""
"1644","Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Shurayh, he said: ""From the third."""
"1645","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Ata, he said: ""From the third."""
"1646","Sa'id said: Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur and Mughirah, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: It is from the third."
"1647","Sa'id said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Hashim and Abu 'Abdullah al-Shaqari, from Ibrahim, he said: ""From the entire wealth."""
"1648","Sa'id said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, from al-Sha'bi, he said: ""From the third."""
"1649","Sa'id said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: ""From the third."""
"1650","Sa'id said: Khalid narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: ""From the third."""
"1651","Sa'id said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: ""From the entire wealth."""
"1652","Chapter: Concerning the mukatab (contractually freed slave) who dies leaving heirs while a remainder of his contract price is due. Sa'id said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Unays ibn Abi Yahya al-Aslami, he said: Men from Quraysh sent me to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib concerning a mukatab jointly owned by them; some of them settled with him (released their share) and some held to their share, then the mukatab died leaving wealth. So Sa'id said to me: ""Those who held to his contract take what is due to them from him, then they divide what remains according to their shares in the mukatab."""
"1653","Sa'id said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Hisn, he said: I disputed before Shurayh concerning a mukatab of mine who died leaving wealth and leaving children, while part of his contract price was still due to me. So Shurayh said to me: ""Take what remains to you of your contract price from what he left, and what remains is for his child, and the wala (clientage) is yours."""
"1654","Sa'id said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning a mukatab who died leaving enough to cover, and he had children, while part of his contract price was still due, he said: ""His masters are given what is due to them of his contract price, and what remains is for his heirs."""
"1655","Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Yusuf, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Yazid informed me that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman judged concerning a man who died leaving a mukatab of his, and the deceased had sons and daughters, then the mukatab died leaving wealth exceeding his contract price, that what remained of the contract price belongs to the men and women among the master's heirs, and whatever wealth there was after that belongs to the men to the exclusion of the women."
"1656","Sa'id said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, he said: 'Umar ibn Ru'bah al-Taghlibi narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Wahid ibn 'Abdullah al-Nasri, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' al-Laythi, he said: ""A woman inherits three inheritances: the inheritance of her freed slave, and her foundling, and the woman who invokes curses (li'an) inherits from her son."""
"1657","Sa'id said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that the Sunnah according to them is that a woman does not inherit from wala (clientage) on behalf of any of her relatives, and that she inherits from wala only what she herself manumitted, or one whom she contracted (for freedom) and who was freed through her, or a client of her client who manumits."
"1658","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan and some of his companions, from Ibrahim, they both said: ""A woman does not inherit from wala except what she manumitted, or what was manumitted by one whom she manumitted."""
"1659","Sa'id said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: ""If a man appoints his mukatab or his slave as executor, that is valid and he has the status of an executor."""
"1660","Sa'id said: Jarir narrated to us from Mughirah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: ""If a man appoints his mukatab as executor, and the mukatab says: I have spent my installments upon my masters, he is believed in that; but if he appoints his slave as executor and he says: I contracted myself and spent my contract price upon my masters, he is not believed in that."""
"1661","Sa'id said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah informed me, from Abu Ma'shar, from al-Nakha'i, concerning a man to whom a gift is sent for a man and he dies, he said: ""Whichever of the two dies, it belongs to the sender of the two, if death occurred before it reached the one to whom it was sent."""
"1662","Sa'id said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from his mother Umm Kulthum, she said: ""When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Umm Salamah, he said to her: I have sent to the Negus ounces of musk and a robe, and I do not think but that he has died, and I do not think my gift which I sent to him except that it will be returned to me; so when it is returned to me, it is yours. So it was as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: the Negus died, and his gift was returned to him; and when the gift was returned to him, he gave every woman among his wives an ounce of that musk, and he gave the rest to Umm Salamah, and he gave her the robe."""
"1663","Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, that three women bought a house and made it for whichever of them remained unmarried, and for whichever of them became poor, and for the last of them to die; then one died, and her heirs disputed with the remaining two before Shurayh, and they told him the story. So Shurayh said: It is not valid; this is ruqba (a conditional life-grant). So he made it subject to the rules of inheritance. End of the Book of Bequests."
"1664","Chapter on encouragement to marry. Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Shadhan informed us, he said: Abu Muhammad Da'laj ibn Ahmad ibn Da'laj al-Sijistani informed us, he said: Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Zayd al-Sa'igh informed us, that Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to them, he said. He said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from 'Ubayd ibn Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves my natural way, let him follow my Sunnah, and part of my Sunnah is marriage."""
"1665","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thabit al-'Abdi narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Ri'ab narrated to us, from Abu Najih, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Poor, poor is a man who has no wife."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he is rich in wealth? He said: ""Even if he is rich in wealth."" And he said: ""Poor, poor, poor is a woman who has no husband."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, even if she is rich in wealth? He said: ""Even if she is rich in wealth."""
"1666","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O company of youths, whoever among you is able to marry, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards the private parts; and whoever is not able, upon him is fasting, for it is a restraint for him."""
"1667","Sa'id narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn 'Amr, the nephew of Anas, narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command marriage and strongly forbid celibacy, and he would say: ""Marry the loving and fertile, for I will boast of your numbers before the Prophets on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1668","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Maysarah narrated to me, he said: Tawus said to me: You shall surely marry, or I shall say to you what 'Umar said to Abu al-Zawa'id: Nothing prevents you from marriage except incapacity or immorality."
"1669","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Nothing like marriage has been seen for two who love one another."""
"1670","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: Ibn Mas'ud said: ""If only ten days remained of my life, and I knew I would die on the last of them, a day in which I had the capacity for marriage, I would marry out of fear of trial."""
"1671","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: He said to me: ""O Sa'id, marry, for the best of this nation were those with the most wives."""
"1672","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn 'Abbas said to me: Marry. I said: That is not in my mind today. He said: If you say that, whatever entrusted seed is in your loins shall surely come forth."
"1673","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, that Ibn 'Abbas called Sumay', Kurayb, and 'Ikrimah, and said to them: ""You have reached what men reach of the matter of women, so whoever among you wishes that I marry him off, I shall marry him off. No man ever commits adultery except that the light of Islam is stripped from him; Allah returns it if He wishes to return it, or withholds it from him if He wishes to withhold it."""
"1674","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, he said: ""The worship-rites (nusuk) of a youth are not complete until he marries."""
"1675","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Shurahbil ibn Muslim al-Khawlani narrated to us, that Abu Muslim al-Khawlani used to say: ""O company of Khawlan, marry off your women and your unmarried ones, for arousal is an overwhelming matter, so prepare provision for it; and know that one who is aroused has no ear (i.e. heeds nothing)."""
"1676","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Shurahbil ibn Muslim narrated to us, that Abu al-Darda used to say: ""Evil helpers toward religion are a cowardly heart, a greedy stomach, and intense arousal."""
"1677","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn 'Amr narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn 'Ubayd al-Hadrami, from Yazid ibn Maysarah, that he used to say: ""How intense is desire in the body; it is but like the blaze of fire, and how shall the continent ones escape it."""
"1678","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best benefit a Muslim man gains after his Islam is a beautiful wife who delights him when he looks at her, obeys him when he commands her, and guards him in his absence regarding his wealth, and herself."""
"1679","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit or Mujahid, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A woman is married for four qualities: for her religion, for her beauty, for her wealth, and for her lineage and ancestry; so take the one with religion, may your hands be dusted."""
"1680","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Makhul, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, he said: ""Four are from the ways of the Messengers: perfuming oneself, modesty, the tooth-stick, and marriage."""
"1681","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, he said: It reached me that the sky is opened for every Muslim man on the night of wedding(?), it is said: he intended chastity from what Allah Almighty forbade."
"1682","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not marry a woman for her beauty, for perhaps her beauty will destroy her; and do not marry a woman for her wealth, for perhaps her wealth will make her transgress; but marry her for her religion. A black, mutilated slave-girl with religion is better than a beautiful woman with no religion."""
"1683","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Burd ibn Sinan, from Makhul, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A woman is married for four: for lineage, religion, wealth, and beauty; so take the one with religion, may your hands be dusted."""
"1684","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Damrah ibn Habib, he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a Bedouin from marrying a Muhajirah woman and taking her out to the desert."""
"1685","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ibn 'Umar intended not to marry, so Hafsah said to him: O my brother, do not do it; marry, for if a child is born to you and they die, they will be a reward for you, and if they live, they will supplicate to Allah Almighty for you."
"1686","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, he said: ""Abu Qilabah used to urge me to the market, and to landed estate, and to seeking the bounty of Allah Almighty, and Muhammad used to urge me to marry."""
"1687","Chapter on marrying virgins. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir and 'Amr ibn Dinar; they both heard Jabir ibn 'Abdullah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Have you married?"" I said: Yes. He said: ""A virgin or a previously married woman?"" I said: Rather a previously married woman. He said: ""Why not a virgin whom you sport with and who sports with you?"" I said: My father was killed on the day of Uhud and left nine daughters, so they are nine sisters to me, and I did not like to bring together with them an inexperienced one like them, and I said: a woman who will look after them and comb their hair. He said: ""You did right."""
"1688","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sayyar informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and when we returned I hurried on a camel of mine that was slow, then a rider caught up with me from behind and prodded my camel with a short spear he had with him, so my camel set off as fine as any camel you ever see. I turned, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Mughirah reported from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir, in this hadith: I turned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is your blessing. Then he returned to the hadith of Sayyar, and he said: ""What hurries you?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am newly wed. He said: ""Did you marry a virgin or a previously married woman?"" I said: Rather a previously married woman. He said: ""Why not a young girl whom you sport with and who sports with you?"" And he said: ""When you come to your family, be shrewd, be shrewd."" When we arrived we set out to enter by day, and he said: ""Wait until we enter by night — that is, in the evening — so that the disheveled one may comb herself, and the one whose husband was absent may remove unwanted hair."""
"1689","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Ubayd al-Kala'i, from 'Amr ibn 'Uthman, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Take to the virgins among women, for they are sweetest of mouths and warmest(?) of skins."""
"1690","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Makhul, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Take to the young maidens, for they are sweetest of mouths, most modest(?) of character, and most open of wombs. Do you not know that I will boast (of your numbers)."""
"1691","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Makhul, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Take to the young maidens and marry them, for they are most open of wombs, most modest(?) of character, and sweetest of mouths. The offspring of the believers — their souls are in green birds in trees in Paradise, cared for by their father Ibrahim, peace and blessings be upon him."""
"1692","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me when I was six years old, and he lived with me (consummated the marriage) when I was nine years old."""
"1693","Chapter on looking at the woman when one wants to marry her. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Bakr ibn 'Abdullah al-Muzani, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him that I had proposed to a woman, and he said: ""Have you seen her?"" I said: No. He said: ""Then look at her, for it is more likely to bring affection between you."" He said: So I came to them and told them what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and her father was with her, and they were both silent. Then the woman said: I adjure you, if the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not command you to look at me, then (do not look); but if the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded you to look at me, then look. And she raised the curtain, so I looked at her and married her; and no woman ever held the place with me that she held, though I married seventy women or some seventy."
"1694","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: 'Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Bakr ibn 'Abdullah al-Muzani, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I proposed to a woman, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Have you looked at her?"" I said: No. He said: ""Then look at her, for it is more likely to bring affection between you."""
"1695","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Bakr ibn 'Abdullah al-Muzani or Abu Qilabah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"1696","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from his uncle Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, he said: I saw Muhammad ibn Maslamah pursuing a woman with his gaze upon a rooftop — she is called Thubaytah bint al-Dahhak, the sister of Abu Jubayrah — and I said: Do you do this while you are a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; when Allah Almighty casts proposing to (a woman) into a man's heart, there is no harm in looking at her."
"1697","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, that 'Umar proposed to 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, for his daughter Umm Kulthum, and 'Ali said: I have reserved my daughters for the sons of Ja'far. He said: Marry her to me, for by Allah there is no man on earth who looks forward to her good companionship as I do. So 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I have married her to you. Then 'Umar came to the gathering of the Muhajirun between the grave and the pulpit — and the Muhajirun would sit there: 'Ali, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, al-Zubayr, 'Uthman, Talhah, and Sa'd — and when in the evening a matter would come to 'Umar from the horizons and he would decide it, he would come to them and tell them of it and consult them all. He said: Congratulate me. They said: For what, O Commander of the Believers? He said: For the daughter of 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him. Then he began telling them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every lineage and tie will be cut off on the Day of Resurrection except my lineage and my tie."" I had accompanied him, and I wished to have that too."
"1698","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Ja'far, he said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, proposed to the daughter of 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he (Ali) mentioned her young age. They said to him: [obscure word in source]. So he repeated his proposal, and he (Ali) said: We shall send her to you to look at her. So he approved of her, and he uncovered her shin, and she said: Let go; were you not the Commander of the Believers, I would have struck your eyes. [Flag: one word in the source is garbled ('innama adrak').]"
"1699","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) congratulated a person on marriage he would say: ""May Allah bless for you, and bless upon you, and join you both in good."""
"1700","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man married a woman from the Ansar, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Look at her, for there is something in the eyes of the Ansar."""
"1701","Chapter on the wedding feast and what has come concerning it. Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: ""The worst food is the food of the wedding feast: the rich are invited to it and the poor are left out; and whoever does not come to the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."""
"1702","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, he said: He said — meaning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever is invited to the wedding feast and does not answer has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."""
"1703","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Bishr ibn 'Asim, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: ""The worst food is the food of the wedding feast: invited to it is one who dislikes it, and barred is one who wants it; the rich are invited to it and the poor are barred from it."""
"1704","Chapter: whoever says there is no marriage except with a guardian. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no marriage except with a guardian."""
"1705","Sa'id narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Any woman married without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is invalid, her marriage is invalid, her marriage is invalid; if he has consummated with her, she gets the dowry for what he made lawful of her private part; and if they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."""
"1706","Sa'id narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same, except that he said: ""If they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."" Isma'il ibn Zakariyya said: Sulayman ibn Musa died fifteen years before al-Zuhri."
"1707","Sa'id narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Jubayr, he said: I heard 'Ikrimah ibn Khalid say: ""A road brought a party of travelers together, and a woman among them appointed a man to manage her affair, and he married her off; so they were raised to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he flogged the one who married and the one who gave in marriage, and separated them."""
"1708","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: ""There is no marriage except with a guardian or a ruler."""
"1709","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Harun al-Sulami informed us, he said: A woman came to Jabir ibn Zayd while he was [garbled phrase in source] of his, and said: Are you Abu al-Sha'tha? He said: Yes. She said: A woman who married herself off? He said: That is a woman whom the Arabs call a prostitute. She said: How foul-mouthed you are, O shaykh. He said: The one who brought foulness is fouler. [Flag: the phrase describing what he was doing is garbled in the source.]"
"1710","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: ""The prostitute is the one who marries herself off without a guardian."""
"1711","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no marriage except with a guardian or the ruler, and the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."""
"1712","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Salim informed us; al-Sha'bi said, when asked about a woman who married while her guardian was absent — al-Sha'bi said: ""If she married unsuitably and unsoundly, her marriage is invalid; but if she married suitably, the matter is up to the guardian: if he wishes he approves, and if he wishes he rejects."""
"1713","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Zakariyya informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about a woman who married while her father was absent, and her husband consummated with her — al-Sha'bi said: ""Since her husband has consummated with her, let her be silent (i.e. remain as she is)."""
"1714","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, he said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab said: ""None marry women off except the guardians, and do not marry them except to suitable matches."""
"1715","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: I asked about a woman who has no guardian — may she marry herself off? He said: ""None marries her off except the guardian."" I said: She has no guardian. He said: Then the ruler; and he refused anything but that."
"1716","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan informed us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When two guardians give in marriage, she is the wife of the first; and when two authorized agents sell, the sale belongs to the first."""
"1717","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan — he said: and I think he raised it (to the Prophet) — that he said the same."
"1718","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: ""The executor has nothing to do with marriage; that belongs only to the guardian."""
"1719","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Harith al-'Ukli, he said: ""Marriage belongs to the guardian, but the executor is consulted."""
"1720","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah, Hushaym, and Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Simak ibn Salamah, he said: I witnessed Shurayh approve the marriage contracted by the executor of the executor of the executor."
"1721","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: I asked Ibrahim about a man who married with the testimony of women, and he said: ""It is not valid, and if it becomes known there is punishment in it; and the minimum that is valid is a suitor and two just witnesses."""
"1722","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, the same, except that he said: ""If they are caught they will be punished; as if to say: the minimum is the suitor and the two witnesses."""
"1723","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us: Sayyar informed us, from Abu Sabrah al-Nakha'i, that 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Hurr al-Ju'fi married a woman from them; her father married her to him, then he went away to Syria and his absence grew long, and the girl's father died, so her brothers and her mother married her off; that reached 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Hurr, so he came and disputed with them about that before 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he judged her to be his; and she was pregnant by the other, so 'Ali placed her in the custody of a trustworthy person until she delivers what is in her womb, then he hands her over to him."
"1724","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: A man in Syria married a woman, and a man here in Kufah married her — and they were two guardians(?) — and 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Hurr al-Ju'fi had married her; so he came from Syria, and they disputed before 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he returned her to him, though she had borne him a child(?) [Flag: pronouns/guardian wording in source is compressed]."
"1725","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, he said: 'Imran ibn Kathir al-Nakha'i informed me that 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Hurr married a young woman from his people called al-Darda; her father married her to him, then 'Ubaydullah went and joined Mu'awiyah and prolonged his absence from his family, and the girl's father died, so her family married her to a man among them called 'Ikrimah; that reached 'Ubaydullah, so he came and disputed with them before 'Ali. When he entered upon 'Ali, he said to him: You joined our enemy and aided against us, and did this and that. He said: Does that prevent me from your justice? He said: No. So they told him their story, and he returned the woman to him, though she was pregnant by 'Ikrimah; so he placed her in the custody of a trustworthy person. The woman said to 'Ali: Am I more entitled to my wealth or is 'Ubaydullah? He said: Rather you are more entitled to it. She said: Then bear witness that whatever dowry of mine was due from 'Ikrimah, it is his. When she delivered what was in her womb, 'Ali returned her to 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Hurr, and he attributed the child to its father."
"1726","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah proposed to the daughter of his uncle 'Urwah ibn Mas'ud al-Thaqafi, so he sent to 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi 'Aqil and said: Marry her to me. He said: I would not do it; you are the governor of the town and her cousin. So he sent to 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As, and he married her to him."
"1727","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Umamah bint Abi al-'As — and her mother was Zaynab bint the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — was with 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him; and when he was struck (killed), Mu'awiyah wrote to Marwan ibn al-Hakam to marry her to him; so Marwan sent to her to entrust her affair to whomever she loved, and she entrusted her affair to al-Mughirah ibn Nawfal ibn al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib. Marwan came with a group of people, and al-Mughirah said to Umamah: Have you entrusted your affair to me? She said: Yes. He said: Then whatever I do in your affair, is it binding? She said: Yes. So al-Mughirah said: He has married her (i.e. I have married her to myself), and I have given her such-and-such dowry. Marwan said to him: That is not yours (to do); we gathered only for you to marry her to the Commander of the Believers. He wrote of that to Mu'awiyah, and Mu'awiyah wrote to him: Leave her and what she is pleased with for herself."
"1728","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Dawud ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Nakha'i informed us, he said: A woman came to Ibrahim and said: The headman of the quarter pursued me and kept at me until I married myself to him. So Ibrahim said: ""That is fornication."""
"1729","Sa'id narrated to us: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Ubayd, he said: Makhul was asked: Is the marriage of a woman whom none owns but herself valid, when she has no father, no brother, and no master? He said: ""It is not valid; rather the imam or a man from the Muslims marries her off."""
"1730","Sa'id narrated to us: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn al-Harith, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: ""There is no marriage except with a guardian or a ruler; but if a disapproved fool gives her in marriage, there is no marriage upon him (i.e. it does not count)."""
"1731","Chapter on seeking the permission of the virgin and the previously married woman. Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The virgin is not to be married until she is asked for permission, nor the previously married woman until she is consulted."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, the virgin is shy. He said: ""Her silence is her consent."""
"1732","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The orphan girl is asked for permission concerning herself, and her silence is her affirmation."""
"1733","Sa'id narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Fadl, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The previously married woman (ayyim) has more right to herself than her guardian, and the virgin is asked for permission concerning herself, and her permission is her silence."""
"1734","Sa'id narrated to us: Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Umar, he said: ""The orphan girl is asked for permission concerning herself; if she is silent, that is her consent, and if she objects, she is not to be married."""
"1735","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: 'Ubaydah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""The orphan girl is not to be married until she is asked for permission, and her silence is her consent."""
"1736","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mujalid informed us: al-Sha'bi narrated to us, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: ""The orphan girl is not to be married until she is asked for permission, and her silence is her consent."""
"1737","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: ""The orphan girl is not to be married until she is asked for permission; if she is silent or weeps, that is her consent, and if she dislikes, she is not to be married."""
"1738","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Ash'ath ibn Sawwar informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Shurayh, that he used to say concerning the orphan girl: ""She is not to be married until she is asked for permission; if she is silent, that is her consent, and if she dislikes and resists, she is not to be married."""
"1739","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us: Hisham ibn Abi 'Abdullah informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Muhajir ibn 'Ikrimah al-Makhzumi, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to marry one of his daughters, he would come to the curtain and say: ""So-and-so mentions such-and-such."""
"1740","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: ""The marriage by the father of his daughter, whether virgin or previously married, is valid."""
"1741","564 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us; Ubaydah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: When a man gives his daughter in marriage, it is valid, whether she is a virgin or previously married."
"1742","565 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from Abd al-Karim, from al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Virgin women are to be consulted concerning themselves; if they refuse, they are given the choice."
"1743","566 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Abi Salamah informed us; Abu Salamah narrated to us that a woman of the Ansar, of Banu Amr ibn Awf, called Khansa bint Khidham, was married by her father to a man while she disliked it, and she was previously married; so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: The matter is yours. She said: I have no need of him. Then she married Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir, and she bore al-Sa'ib ibn Abi Lubabah."
"1744","567 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah informed us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, that Khansa bint Khidham was married by her father though she had charge of her own affair, and she disliked that man; so she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, my father married me to a man I do not want. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your affair is in your hand. Then Abu Lubabah proposed to her and married her, and she bore al-Sa'ib ibn Abi Lubabah."
"1745","568 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father, and an excellent father he is, was approached by my son's uncle seeking my hand and he turned him away, and married me to a man while I disliked it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for her father and asked him about her statement; he said: She spoke the truth; I married her off and sought only good for her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have no marriage; go and marry whomever you wish. [Flag: text ends abruptly in source, closing quote missing.]"
"1746","569 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, who said: When the orphan girl is proposed to and she remains silent, that is her consent; but if she dislikes it, then she has not consented."
"1747","570 - Sa'id narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us; Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him that a man married off a daughter of his while she disliked it, and she grew up intending to assert herself; so that was raised to Uthman ibn Affan, and he annulled his marriage."
"1748","571 - Sa'id narrated to us; Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, who said: A man may give his daughter in marriage without consulting her when she is under his care; but when she lives apart on her own with her household and children, he consults her."
"1749","572 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, who said: When a man marries off his son while he is small, there is no choice for him."
"1750","573 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, saying: One of his companions informed us, from Ibrahim, the same as that."
"1751","574 - Sa'id narrated to us; Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Hawshab, from Ikrimah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not compel women into what they dislike."
"1752","575 - Sa'id narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'bad ibn Umayr, nephew of Ubayd ibn Umayr, that Umar ibn al-Khattab annulled the marriage of a woman who married without a guardian."
"1753","576 - Sa'id narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Mujammi' ibn Yazid, who said: Khidham married off his daughter while she disliked it, so she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father married me off while I disliked it, in a strange land. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled her marriage."
"1754","577 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Muhajir ibn Ikrimah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated a virgin woman from her husband; her father had married her off without her permission. He said: And I was told that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wished to marry one of his daughters, he would sit beside her curtain and say: So-and-so mentions so-and-so. [Flag: text breaks off mid-sentence in source.]"
"1755","578 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, who said: Maternal uncles of a woman, who were of Banu A'idh Allah, married her off, while she was of Banu Awd; so they came to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said to his daughter Umm Kulthum: See, is she a grown woman? She said: Yes. So he handed her to her husband and said: They are suitable matches."
"1756","579 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: al-Shaybani informed us, from Abu Qays, that a woman of A'idh Allah called Salamah bint Ubayd was married off by her mother and her family; so that was raised to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: Has she not already been entered unto? Then the marriage is valid."
"1757","580 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Abu Qays al-Awdi, from one who informed him, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he upheld the marriage of a woman whom her mother had married off with her consent."
"1758","581 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Abu Ja'far al-Ashja'i, that a woman wished to marry but her guardian prevented her, so she appealed to Shurayh, who said: Permit her marriage. He seemed to delay, so Shurayh said: Give permission before you have no permission left. Then Shurayh married her off."
"1759","582 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus ibn Ubayd informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, that Ziyad sent Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa over some charities and said to him: I place you and myself regarding this wealth in the position of the guardian of the orphan: whoever is rich, let him abstain, and whoever is poor, let him consume in a fair manner; and do not come upon any shighar marriage without annulling it, nor any woman whose guardian withholds her from marriage so that she remains apart, her tether abandoned, without marrying her to suitable matches among her people."
"1760","583 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, who said: A man came to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: O Commander of the Believers, what is my affair and that of my orphan girl? He said: About which of you two do you ask? Then he said to him: Are you yourself marrying her, she being rich and beautiful? He said: Yes, by God. He said: Then marry her off homely and without wealth; it is better for her; and if it is someone other than you for her, then give her the choice."
"1761","Chapter on marriage compatibility. 584 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us; al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, saying: Ibrahim al-Taymi narrated to me, saying: Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah have mercy on him, said to a woman of his family: I adjure you by Allah to marry a Muslim, even if he is a red Roman or a black Abyssinian."
"1762","585 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I married Zayd ibn Harithah to Zaynab bint Jahsh, and I married al-Miqdad to Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib, so that they may know that the noblest nobility is Islam."
"1763","586 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughirah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Bilal proposed on behalf of his brother to a household of the Arabs, saying: I am Bilal and this is my brother; we were two slaves and Allah freed us, and we were astray and Allah guided us."
"1764","587 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Abu Sufyan, freedman of Muzaynah, informed us that Bilal said: If you marry us, praise be to Allah; and if you turn us away, Allah is Greatest."
"1765","588 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from al-Hakam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Suhayb to propose to some people of the Ansar; so he came to them and proposed, and they said: We will not marry you, a slave; and they disdained him. He said: Were it not that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me, I would not have done it. They said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) order you? He said: Yes. They said: Then her affair is in your hand. So they married her to him, and he informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then some gold came to him, and he ordered for him a piece of gold and said to him: Drive this to your family. And he said to his Companions: Contribute for your brother for his wedding feast."
"1766","589 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm, who said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman and I entered upon Fatimah bint Qays, and I said to her: How did your husband divorce you? She said: He divorced me with an irrevocable divorce, and gave me neither lodging nor maintenance. Then he said: He spoke the truth. And he ordered me to observe my waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum; then he said: I have learned that Ibn Umm Maktum is a man frequently visited, but observe your waiting period in the house of so-and-so. When my waiting period ended, Mu'awiyah and Abu al-Jahm proposed to me, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mu'awiyah has no wealth, and Abu al-Jahm is harsh toward women; but I will marry you to Usamah. She said: So he married me to Usamah, and I was blessed in him."
"1767","590 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Ibn Hurmuz al-San'ani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When there comes to you one whose religion and trustworthiness you approve, marry him off; unless you do, there will be tribulation in the land and great corruption. They said: O Messenger of Allah, even if so and so? He said: Yes."
"1768","591 - Muhammad narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: Asma bint Abi Bakr said to us: O my sons and sons of my sons, this marriage is a kind of bondage, so let each of you look to whom he bonds his noble girl."
"1769","592 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: When Salman proposed to Abu Qurrah al-Kindi, and he entered upon her, he said: What is this? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) charged me, saying: If Allah decrees for you to marry, let the first thing you unite upon be obedience to Allah. She said: You have sat in the seat of one whose command is obeyed. He said to her: Stand and pray, and we shall supplicate. They did so; then he saw a curtained house and said: What is with this house of yours? Is it feverish, or has the Ka'bah moved to Kindah? They said: It is not feverish, nor has the Ka'bah moved to Kindah. He said: I will not enter it until every curtain is torn down except a curtain over a door."
"1770","593 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Layla al-Kindi, who said: Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, went out with thirteen men of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; when the prayer came, they said: Step forward, O Abu Abdullah, for you are the most knowledgeable and eldest of us. He said: Allah has favored you over us, O company of Arabs: you lead us and we do not lead you, and you marry our women and we do not marry your women. Then a man of the people stepped forward and prayed four with them; when he finished, Salman said to him: You prayed four; we were in greater need of the concession."
"1771","593 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Layla al-Kindi, who said: Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, went out with thirteen men of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; when the prayer came, they said: Step forward, O Abu Abdullah, for you are the most knowledgeable and eldest of us. He said: Allah has favored you over us, O company of Arabs: you lead us and we do not lead you, and you marry our women and we do not marry your women. Then a man of the people stepped forward and prayed four with them; when he finished, Salman said to him: You prayed four; we were in greater need of the concession."
"1772","594 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Aws ibn Dam'aj say: Salman said: We do not lead you, nor do we marry your women."
"1773","Chapter on dowry. 595 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, who said: I heard it from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who heard it from Abu al-Ajfa al-Sulami, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, say: Beware, do not go to excess in women's dowries, for had it been an honor among people or piety with Allah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have been most entitled to it among you; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not marry any of his wives nor marry any of his daughters for more than twelve uqiyah; yet one of you inflates his wife's dowry until it becomes enmity in his heart, saying to her: I burdened myself for you with the water-skin's suspension. He said: I was young and did not know what the suspension of the water-skin was. And another thing you say in your campaigns: So-and-so was killed a martyr, though perhaps he loaded the back of his mount or its rump with silver or gold seeking the world; rather say as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed in the path of Allah is a martyr."
"1774","596 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mansur informed us, from Ibn Sirin, who said: Abu al-Ajfa al-Sulami narrated to us, saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, addressing the people; he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Beware, do not go to excess in women's dowries, for had it been an honor in this world or piety with Allah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have been most entitled to it; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give any of his wives more than twelve uqiyah, nor was any of his daughters given more than twelve uqiyah; yet one of you inflates a woman's dowry until she is left with enmity in his heart, saying: I burdened myself for you with the water-skin's suspension or sweat; and another thing you say in your campaigns: So-and-so was killed a martyr, and so-and-so died a martyr, though perhaps he loaded his mount's back or rump with gold or silver, seeking dinars and dirhams; so do not say that, but say as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies in the path of Allah or is killed is a martyr."
"1775","597 - Sa'id narrated to us; Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Salamah ibn Alqamah, Ayyub, Ibn Awn and Hisham informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin: as for Salamah he said: I was told of Abu al-Ajfa, and the others said: From Abu al-Ajfa, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Beware, do not go to excess in women's dowries, for had it been an honor in this world or piety with Allah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have been most entitled to it; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give any of his wives, nor was any of his daughters given, more than twelve uqiyah; yet a man inflates his wife's dowry until she is left with enmity in his heart, saying: I burdened myself for you with the water-skin's suspension; I was a young Arab lad and did not know what the suspension of the water-skin was; and another thing you say in these campaigns of yours: So-and-so was killed a martyr, though perhaps he loaded his mount's or beast's rump with silver and gold seeking trade; so do not say that, but say as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed in the path of Allah is in Paradise. Ismail said: The narration of one of them entered into another's."
"1776","598 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed the people, praised Allah and extolled Him, and said: Beware, do not go to excess in women's dowries, for if I learn of anyone who pays more than what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid or was paid to him, I shall place the excess in the public treasury. Then he descended, and a woman of Quraysh confronted him, saying: O Commander of the Believers, is Allah's Book more deserving to be followed, or your word? He said: Allah's Book; what is that? She said: A moment ago you forbade people to go to excess in women's dowries, while Allah says in His Book: And you have given one of them a qintar, take nothing of it. Umar said: Everyone is more understanding than Umar, twice or thrice; then he returned to the pulpit and said to the people: I had forbidden you to go to excess in women's dowries; now let a man do with his wealth as he pleases."
"1777","599 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: I set out intending to forbid you excess in dowry, until this verse confronted me: And you have given one of them a qintar, take nothing of it."
"1778","600 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from a man who heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I wished to propose to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his daughter; I remembered I had nothing, then I remembered his kindness and kinship, so I proposed to him and he said: Do you have anything? I said: No. He said: Where is your Hutami armor? I said: It is with me. He said: Bring it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her to me; on the night I entered upon her, he came and sat while we were in a blanket; when we saw him we drew ourselves together before him, and he said: Do nothing until I come to you. Then he called for a vessel with water, supplicated in it, sprinkled it upon us, and said; I said: O Messenger of Allah, am I dearer to you or she? He said: She is dearer to me than you, and you are more honored to me than she."
"1779","601 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mujalid ibn Sa'id, saying: I was informed by one who heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say upon the pulpit: I married the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we had no bed to sleep on but a sheepskin, on which we slept by night and on which we fed the water-carrying camel by day."
"1780","602 - Sa'id narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Ikrimah, who said: Ali made Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, lawful with a body of iron."
"1781","603 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not marry any of his wives nor marry any of his daughters for more than twelve and a half uqiyah."
"1782","604 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, that Abu Hadrad al-Aslami married a woman and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking help with her dowry; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How much have you given her? He said: Two hundred dirhams. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you scooped it from the water of But-han, you would have added more."
"1783","605 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, who said: They disliked free women's dowries being like prostitutes' wages, that a man marry for one or two dirhams; he liked it to be twenty dirhams. [Flag: source has uncertainty marks around the number twenty.]"
"1784","606 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah informed us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, that he liked the dowry to be forty dirhams."
"1785","607 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Husam ibn Misakk informed us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that he liked the dowry to be fifty dirhams."
"1786","608 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: It is upon whatever they mutually agree, little or much, and he fixed nothing."
"1787","609 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas, that Abd al-Rahman married a woman for the weight of a date-stone in gold, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Give a feast, even with a sheep."
"1788","610 - Sa'id narrated to us; Abu Awanah and Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, who said: The sunnah concerning dowry is a ritl of silver."
"1789","611 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a yellow trace on Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and said: What is this? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I married a woman for the weight of a date-stone in gold. He said: May Allah bless you; give a feast, even with a sheep."
"1790","612 - Sa'id narrated to us; Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married a woman for the weight of a date-stone in gold."
"1791","613 - Sa'id narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us; Hajjaj narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said, he said: It was valued at three dirhams. [Flag: terse in source; pronoun reference unclear.]"
"1792","614 - Sa'id narrated to us; Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, who said: Whatever they mutually agree upon is dowry."
"1793","615 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Habib ibn Ubayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contract of manumission nor dowry from which nothing is remitted but it is accursed."
"1794","616 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hariz ibn Uthman, from the elders, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contract of manumission, nor dowry, nor blood-money from which nothing is remitted but it is accursed."
"1795","617 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, that Ibn Abbas married Shumaylah al-Sulamiyyah for ten thousand."
"1796","618 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, that he married a woman for ten thousand in full."
"1797","619 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym and Abu Shihab narrated to us, both saying together: Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah al-Ta'ifi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Marry the unmarried among you, marry the unmarried among you. Sa'id said: Hushaym said it twice, and Abu Shihab said it three times. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the ties between them? He said: Whatever their families mutually agree upon."
"1798","620 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Yasar ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib married his daughter to his brother's son for two dirhams."
"1799","Chapter on a man marrying a woman leaving it to her judgment. 621 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Salim informed us, saying: I heard al-Sha'bi say: When a man marries a woman leaving it to her judgment or her family's judgment, and she or the judge acts unjustly, that is referred back to the dowry of her peers, with neither loss nor excess."
"1800","622 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Amr ibn Hurayth proposed to Adi ibn Hatim for his daughter, but he refused to marry her to him except leaving it to his judgment; Amr disliked it, fearing he would judge against him his house or something severing him; then he decided to marry her to him on his judgment, so Adi said to him: I shall not judge a judgment for which Allah will question me on the Day of Resurrection; then he judged twelve uqiyah, four hundred and eighty dirhams."
